rs/hctsaik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hctsaik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hctsaik/nativeApp/commits/9a60cab2ff705af0ee73d236c0556e282a575094/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T14:29:21Z","email":"36671829+hctsaik@users.noreply.github.com","name":"hctsaik"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T14:29:21Z","email":"36671829+hctsaik@users.noreply.github.com","name":"hctsaik"},"message":"docs(WDAC): correct conclusion — prebuilt Tauri exe RUNS; only rebuild is blocked\n\nEmpirically (2026-06-29) the already-built cim-light.exe (Tauri shell) launches fine\nunder WDAC (portal + engine load); only fresh cargo compiles (tauri dev/build''s new\nbuild-script exe) are blocked (os error 4551). So the earlier \"local Tauri is not\nviable, stay on Electron\" was wrong.\n\n- CLAUDE.md「## WDAC」: key distinction is \"newly-compiled unsigned exe blocked vs\n  running an existing exe is fine\"; local DEV mainline = run the prebuilt cim-light.exe\n  (never `tauri dev`/`tauri build` locally); day-to-day dev edits portal/engine/modules\n  (runtime-loaded, no Rust rebuild); rebuild the shell elsewhere only when needed;\n  Electron-nowdac is the final fallback.\n- start-dev-tauri.bat: run the existing cim-light.exe directly (release|debug), set\n  CIM_ENGINE_EXE/CIM_ENGINE_PYTHON for the source engine; fall back to Electron-nowdac\n  only if no prebuilt exe exists. No more `npm run tauri:dev` (which triggers the blocked\n  cargo rebuild).\n- docs/platform/startup-tauri.md: same correction.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fc87bd1cd4af54ff6437f43d41e33dcc347d0fc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hctsaik/nativeApp/git/trees/fc87bd1cd4af54ff6437f43d41e33dcc347d0fc1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hctsaik/nativeApp/git/commits/9a60cab2ff705af0ee73d236c0556e282a575094","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","sig