api.github.com/users/syedhaffiz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syedhaffiz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syedhaffiz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syedhaffiz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syedhaffiz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/syedhaffiz/didactic-octo-happiness/commits/654005b8616c56b570bbff2a530174ca6f47f9af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-02T03:28:45Z","email":"haffizsyed@gmail.com","name":"Syed Haffiz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-02T03:28:45Z","email":"haffizsyed@gmail.com","name":"Syed Haffiz"},"message":"Stabilize useApi refs and cancellation\n\nRefactor useApi to use refs for the fetch function and cache flag so the effect won''t restart on every render while still reading the latest values. Introduce readCache and initialize state from the cache lazily. Replace the shared callId counter with a per-effect cancelled flag to avoid races (fixes issues with StrictMode double-invoke and reused in-flight promises) and ensure cleanup on unmount/refetch. Keep in-flight dedupe behavior and only key the effect on [key, tick].","tree":{"sha":"e26ae2786928565cf214d76ced6d67d1c3a4d01e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/syedhaffiz/didactic-octo-happiness/git/trees/e26ae2786928565cf214d76ced6d67d1c3a4d01e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/syedhaffiz/didactic-octo-happiness/git/commits/654005b8616c56b570bbff2a530174ca6f47f9af","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25886784?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syedhaffiz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syedhaffiz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syedhaffiz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://ap