","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syedhaffiz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syedhaffiz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syedhaffiz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/syedhaffiz/didactic-octo-happiness/commits/e39c8740d1d0db740eb1522e72fd576dfe0ee134/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T03:31:14Z","email":"haffizsyed@gmail.com","name":"Syed Haffiz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T03:31:14Z","email":"haffizsyed@gmail.com","name":"Syed Haffiz"},"message":"Add per-index range & single-index API\n\nIntroduce a per-index API and UI so each index card can control its own range independently. Backend: add GET /inventory/index/{code} (controller, route, service, repository), update mocks with buildOneIndex, and document the endpoint in OpenAPI with 404 handling. Frontend: add inventory.indexOne and mock, refactor IndexPage to perform one bulk fetch for default-range data and render per-card PriceIndexCard components that store their range in a URL param (slugged key) and refetch only when the user selects a non-default range; show loading on per-card refetches. This reduces unnecessary re-fetching and allows each card''s range dropdown to be independent.","tree":{"sha":"20fb291a31ec96670ecf973f5f2a39ffcd61c67f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/syedhaffiz/didactic-octo-happiness/git/trees/20fb291a31ec96670ecf973f5f2a39ffcd61c67f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/syedhaffiz/didactic-octo-happiness/git/commits/e39c8740d1d0db740eb1522e72fd576dfe0ee134","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25886784?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syedhaffiz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syedhaffiz/followers","following_url":"https://ap