nt.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/0cd98cf734f9976af823bc84ec49f11fb914695a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:00:09Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T09:01:55Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"fix(chart): no credential is minted or carried by the render, and ESO is a prerequisite the render checks (XC-004)\n\nEvery credential the chart used to render or read from a value now lives in the secret store and\nreaches a pod from it: the Dapr secret store for a sidecar, an ExternalSecret for a pod without one.\n\n- ESO is a prerequisite rask never installs (owner, 2026-10-05). external-secrets.yaml always renders\n  and fails the render, naming the operator, when the cluster does not serve external-secrets.io/v1\n  (`.Capabilities`; a cluster-less render passes --api-versions). It also refuses a render with no store.\n  `externalSecrets.enabled` is gone with its ESO-off path: infra-credentials.yaml, the static\n  observability-s3 and ray-auth-token Secrets (and the randAlphaNum mint behind the latter).\n- The dev OpenBao''s credentials are generated in-cluster: ESO''s Password generator fills\n  `<release>-dev-credentials` once (CreatedOnce, resource-policy keep) with minio-secret-key,\n  postgres-password, dapr-app-token, ray-auth-token and frontend-session-secret. The OpenBao pod mounts\n  it and the seed writes every field as `@file`; the scoped storage secrets (and the multibase fixture''s,\n  e394ddbf) are derived in-cluster from the root by one helper, `lance.scopedSecretFn`, in the seed and in\n  minio-scoped-users, whose Job now takes the root and every derived secret as memory files (no env\n  literal). It persists in a Secret rather than only the in-memory store because AGE and the object store\n  keep what they were initialised with across an OpenBao replacement. The seed re-reads the mounted Secret\n  (and the operator''s hf-token) every 5 s and re-seeds when it changes, so a rotation never replaces the\n  OpenBao pod, which without a surge would re-mint the signing pairs and the NATS root.\n- An estate whose AGE or object-store StatefulSet exists without `<release>-dev-credentials` is refused\n  (`lookup`, against a cluster only): generating beside live data would lock every consumer out. The\n  operator creates the Secret from the credentials the estate holds, and a Secret without an owner is\n  operator-held, so no generator renders beside it. This is what lets the first upgrade change no\n  credential and converge under --wait; rotation is a separate, ordered step (OPERATORS.md 8).\n- dapr-app-token.yaml, the frontend-session Secret and secrets.yaml''s HF_TOKEN are deleted; ESO writes\n  `<release>-dapr-app-token`, `<release>-frontend-session` and (with secrets.hfTokenInStore)\n  `<release>-hf-token` from the store. The HF token is operator-supplied: make k3s-up writes the\n  bootstrap Secret `rask-supplied-credentials` from HF_TOKEN on stdin and the seed stores it.\n- prod-credentials.yaml refuses, on every render, any credential passed as a value (dapr.appToken,\n  frontend.oidc.sessionSecret, secrets.hfToken, ray.auth.token, age.password, minio.secretKey and the six\n  minio.*SecretKey), naming them. The two exemptions (owner, 2026-10-06), the bundled dev Dex''s\n  configuration (XC-025) and the dev OpenBao root token (XC-079), are fenced to dev renders: a real\n  deployment refuses the dev OpenBao and the bundled Dex (values-prod.yaml turns Dex off), so the chart\n  never generates for one. The no-store `value:` env branches (catalog, lineage, medallion x2, maintenance x2,\n  explorer) are removed: with no value left, the store is the only source.\n- Makefile: k3s-up/k3s-converge no longer pass sessionSecret, hfToken or minio.secretKey, and drop the\n  carried credential keys from the re-fed live values with `--set <key>=null`.\n- The e2e stacks install ESO 2.10.0 on their throwaway kind cluster (standing in for the platform);\n  prod_render_check, the Dagger render args and the docs (deployment.md prerequisites, OPERATORS.md § 8,\n  chart README, DEPLOY.md, DURABILITY.md) follow; rask-helm and rask-dapr skills corrected.\n- Removing the checksum annotations of ESO-owned Secrets means a rotation rolls nothing on its own;\n  OPERATORS.md 8 orders each rotation (key, re-seed, force-sync every ExternalSecret reading the store,\n  the server, then its consumers, the Ray head included) and forbids deleting the OpenBao pod. The\n  carry-forward, husk deletion and every rotation are live steps.\n\nRelease size: a values-local render packed as Helm stores it (Python gzip-9, manifest + templates)\nshrinks by 9,844 bytes (936,692 -> 926,848).\n\nTests: +7 -10 (cases).\n+ test_no_credential_is_carried_by_the_render.py: two cluster-less renders are byte-identical (x2\n  overlays), a credential value is refused naming it, a real deployment refuses the bundled dev IdP, a\n  render without ESO fails naming it.\n+ test_the_dev_openbao_is_seeded_by_its_own_pod.py: two cases (a store missing a generated credential is\n  never Ready; a rotated credential and hf-token reach the store in place, keeping the signing pairs and the\n  bus root); the test now also runs the seed with generated files and the Job''s derive step and\n  asserts every service''s scoped field holds the secret the Job gives its access key, never the root.\n- test_a_rotated_secret_reaches_the_pods_that_hold_it.py (2) and test_a_sidecar_given_a_token_carries_its_checksum.py\n  (1): their claim (a chart-rendered Secret''s checksum) has no subject once ESO owns the Secret.\n- test_a_scoped_identity_needs_only_its_name.py (2): its pairing moved into the seed test, as its own\n  comment directed.\n- test_ray_auth.py: the ESO-ownership test (1) and the static/ESO parametrize twins (2); the\n  no-store signing case (1) and the no-ESO NATS case (1), both now render refusals.\nSubset-twin check over the seam (the new file, the seed test, test_ray_auth, test_secret_env_delivery,\ntest_invariants, the kube-api and Dapr-component gates): union of executed production lines 3,323 over the\nkept set; the deleted tests only shell out to helm, so they ran no production Python line (read, not\nmeasured before deletion) and the union cannot have shrunk; the only twin\ncandidates are three untouched test_invariants bucket cases, outside this seam. Baselines lowered:\nSECRET_ENV_BASELINE 23 -> 22, PLAINTEXT_SECRET_BASELINE 6 -> 0 (pins no Job literal).\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"a66528c9be75daca587b930ebf894b9239200332","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/a66528c9be75daca587b930ebf894b9239200332"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/0cd98cf734f9976af823bc84ec49f11fb914695a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_ur