tps://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/6c5368e0b6c09050aaaab7badb3689272cd34d5d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:16:15Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:16:15Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"docs(register): park the eight rules the prune left without a behavioural test (LH-428)\n\nf0c997f9 deleted 30 source-reading tests under CLAUDE.md''s rule; eight were the only check on a\nreal rule. They are parked, uncounted, to be pinned through their doors when each seam is next touched.\n\ntests: +0 −0\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"27d7b80f808c7f42a004020cb2e4be754a771434","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/27d7b80f808c7f42a004020cb2e4be754a771434"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/6c5368e0b6c09050aaaab7badb3689272cd34d5d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/6c5368e0b6c09050aaaab7badb3689272cd34d5d","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKDZjNTM2OGUwYjZjMDkwNTBhYWFhYjdiYWRiMzY4OTI3MmNkMzRkNWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/f0c997f983e9c88066f61f448f3475954a454ac2","sha":"f0c997f983e9c88066f61f448f3475954a454ac2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/f0c997f983e9c88066f61f448f3475954a454ac2"}],"sha":"6c5368e0b6c09050aaaab7badb3689272cd34d5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/6c5368e0b6c09050aaaab7badb3689272cd34d5d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/f0c997f983e9c88066f61f448f3475954a454ac2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:10:06Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:13:45Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"test: prune twins, source readers and library checks from the 10-04+ seams (owner 2026-10-06)\n\nScope: every test file added or changed since 2026-10-04 (185 live files), measured per member\ntogether with the rest of that member''s suite and the tests/unit + tests/integration files that import\nit. testing-python pruning.md steps 1-4: per-test |run coverage (-n 8), the zero-line finder, the\nsubset-twin finder, then both tests'' asserts read before either was deleted.\n\nUnion of |run production lines per scope, before -> after (any-phase union in brackets):\n  catalog        1895 -> 1882 tests   14647 -> 14647   [30930 -> 30930]\n  medallion       866 ->  862 tests   10989 -> 10989   [22886 -> 22886]\n  maintenance     577 ->  564 tests   11028 -> 11028   [18081 -> 18081]\n  service-kit     718 ->  714 tests   12939 -> 12938   [19749 -> 19748]\n  ingest          487 ->  480 tests    7423 ->  7423   [19259 -> 19259]\n  notifications   610 ->  603 tests    5420 ->  5303   [14622 -> 14622]\nThe catalog baseline was measured twice with identical line sets. Both differences are attribution,\nnot lost coverage. notifications: the 117 lines are the module-level import of\nannotator/api/v1/endpoints/project_events.py; they still run, now in a fixture''s setup phase instead\nof test_task_assignment_reaches_the_inbox''s run phase. service-kit: otel.py:201 is the \"logger\nprovider already bound\" branch. Its only executor before and after is test_otel''s\ntest_NO_settings_still_opts_in_through_the_endpoint, and it runs whenever another setup_otel call\nprecedes it in the worker (shown running test_otel.py serially).\n\nDeleted twins (kept test covers the lines and asserts; red check = the mutation applied to production,\nkept test red on its own assertion, green once restored):\n- services/notifications/tests/test_reconciler.py::test_an_unreachable_store_is_unreadable_never_absent\n  kept ::test_an_unreadable_cursor_stops_the_tick_rather_than_re_priming\n  red: reconciler.py cursor read returns None instead of raising LineageCursorUnreadable\n- services/notifications/tests/test_reconciler.py::test_paging_older_passes_the_cursor_as_after\n  kept ::test_the_next_tick_resumes_the_descent_instead_of_restarting\n  red: reconciler.py page() sends the cursor as `before`\n- packages/lineage-kit/tests/test_config.py::test_auto_transport_with_endpoint_is_http\n  kept ::test_each_emit_presents_the_identity_token_the_file_holds_at_that_moment\n  red: emitter.py auto transport always \"noop\"\n- packages/lineage-kit/tests/test_config.py::test_auto_transport_without_endpoint_is_noop\n  kept packages/lineage-kit/tests/test_noop.py::test_full_pipeline_shape_runs_unlineaged_without_crashing\n  red: emitter.py auto transport without an endpoint is \"console\"\n- services/medallion/tests/test_a_train_feature_resolves_where_the_catalog_says.py::test_an_unregistered_feature_still_reaches_the_job_by_its_composed_path\n  kept tests/unit/test_train.py::test_consumer_submits_and_acks_and_maps_outcomes\n  red: train.py no-catalog fallback returns a different path\n- services/medallion/tests/test_the_order_is_the_one_serialization.py::test_the_workloads_parameters_ride_the_ORDER\n  kept tests/unit/test_medallion.py::test_a_lane_cannot_reach_a_platform_variable_by_colliding_on_its_name\n  red: work_order.py to_env renames the RASK_PARAM_ prefix\n- services/catalog/tests/test_control_events_survive_a_bus_outage.py::test_a_failed_control_publish_leaves_the_event_STAGED\n  kept services/catalog/tests/test_the_control_lane_has_a_relay.py::test_the_relay_REPUBLISHES_a_staged_table_published\n  red: control_emit.py publishes with an empty outbox_uri\n- services/catalog/tests/test_a_consumer_can_read_changes_since_a_version.py::test_a_deleted_row_COMES_BACK_from_the_transaction_range\n  kept services/catalog/tests/test_the_change_feed_answers_only_what_lance_records.py::test_a_window_is_answered_only_where_the_version_columns_describe_it[compaction]\n  red: dataplane.py deleted-row reader yields no batches (same schema)\n- tests/unit/test_format_guard.py::test_allows_lance_or_absent[None]\n  kept tests/unit/test_a_namespace_create_mode_means_what_the_spec_says.py::test_exist_ok_on_a_free_id_still_creates_AND_seeds[asyncio]\n  red: formats.py raises on non-mapping properties\n- services/ingest/tests/test_blob_placement_thresholds.py::TestTheBronzeSchemaCarriesThem::test_the_payload_field_records_both_thresholds\n  kept ::TestTheBronzeSchemaCarriesThem::test_the_recorded_values_are_the_named_constants\n  red: runtime.py bronze payload field drops inline_size_threshold\n- services/maintenance/tests/test_a_refused_plan_request_is_the_executors_bug.py::test_an_unavailable_plane_stays_an_outage[500]\n  kept ::test_an_unavailable_plane_still_falls_back_in_pod (the 503 on the same >= 400 branch)\n  red: catalog_compaction.py raises CompactionPlanRefused on a 5xx\n- tests/unit/test_maintenance_lineage.py::test_make_emitter_is_noop_when_disabled_and_dapr_when_wired[enabled-and-wired]\n  kept services/maintenance/tests/test_the_sweep_signs_what_it_emits.py::test_every_event_the_service_emits_is_authored_and_signed_as_the_service[a-compaction]\n  red: lineage_emit.py make_emitter never builds the Dapr emitter\n  (the surviving [disabled] case is renamed test_make_emitter_is_noop_when_disabled)\n\nDeleted library-behaviour checks (pylance''s own behaviour, which rask passes explicitly or no longer\ndepends on):\n- services/ingest/tests/test_blob_placement_thresholds.py::TestTheNamedThresholdsAreTheOnesLanceApplies::test_the_pinned_values_still_match_lances_own_defaults\n- services/ingest/tests/test_blob_placement_thresholds.py::TestTheNamedThresholdsAreTheOnesLanceApplies::test_dedicated_is_evaluated_BEFORE_inline\n- tests/unit/test_blob_null_alignment.py::test_upstream_fixed_the_null_drop_and_the_shape_changed_with_it\n\nDeleted change-detector (compares mounted routes against two lists that live only in the test):\n- tests/unit/test_a_maintenance_door_that_mints_a_version_records_who_did_it.py::test_every_mounted_maintenance_verb_is_classified\n\nDeleted readers of source text or an AST (inspect.getsource, ast.parse, read_text plus regex). None of\nthese rules can be written as a ruff banned-api entry or an import-linter contract (keyword wiring,\ncall order, string content, log fields), so per CLAUDE.md the expression is nowhere:\n- services/catalog/tests/test_a_data_read_is_audited.py::test_every_data_read_door_records_who_read_it\n- services/catalog/tests/test_a_multibase_table_falls_back_only_for_the_bases_the_policy_misses.py::test_describe_with_vending_scopes_the_credential_to_the_TABLE_not_less\n- services/catalog/tests/test_a_singular_record_read_refuses_what_it_cannot_parse.py::test_every_singular_reader_validates_what_it_returns\n- services/catalog/tests/test_a_warehouse_cascade_revokes_its_tables.py::test_the_cascade_actually_calls_it_and_before_the_drop\n- services/catalog/tests/test_publish_override.py::TestTheOverrideNeedsAHigherRungThanPublishItself::test_the_route_requires_can_promote_when_assertions_are_accepted\n- services/catalog/tests/test_routes_declare_only_what_they_use.py::test_no_route_declares_a_dependency_its_body_never_uses\n  (ruff ARG001 would express a broader form of this rule; not enabled here)\n- tests/unit/test_warehouse_adopt_existing.py::test_adoption_never_bypasses_the_hazard_guards\n- tests/unit/test_warehouse_adopt_existing.py::test_adoption_branch_converges_only_the_warehouse_root_conflict\n- services/medallion/tests/test_run_doors_refuse_while_draining.py::TestEveryHttpRunDoorIsGated::test_it_depends_on_the_http_refusal[produce.py-produce]\n- tests/unit/test_the_submitter_and_the_job_agree_on_the_wire.py::test_every_name_the_job_reads_is_one_the_ORDER_supplies\n- services/notifications/tests/test_lane_parity.py::test_every_lane_forwards_the_watcher_lookup\n- services/notifications/tests/test_lane_parity.py::test_every_lane_forwards_the_channel_push\n- services/lineage/tests/test_an_unresolvable_source_names_its_producer.py::test_the_SHARED_SEAM_reports_it_rather_than_one_door\n- services/lineage/tests/test_the_runs_of_one_cascade_are_joinable.py::test_BOTH_readers_declare_the_same_column_count_as_the_projection\n- services/maintenance/tests/test_a_deliberately_empty_field_is_not_a_missing_one.py::test_the_TRASH_registry_is_the_call_site_that_asks_for_both_rules\n- services/maintenance/tests/test_a_denied_rewrite_is_refused_not_root_signed.py::test_both_refusal_sites_use_the_one_wording\n- services/maintenance/tests/test_a_rewrite_reports_what_it_costs_the_process.py::test_a_committed_rewrite_reports_RESIDENT_BYTES\n- services/maintenance/tests/test_a_worker_retires_before_it_is_killed.py::test_every_module_that_holds_a_rewrite_slot_also_counts_the_pass\n- services/maintenance/tests/test_cron_router_is_built_not_imported.py::test_a_dry_run_PLAN_is_reported_as_loudly_as_a_reclamation\n- services/maintenance/tests/test_cron_router_is_built_not_imported.py::test_the_drift_report_NAMES_its_findings_and_not_only_counts_them\n- services/maintenance/tests/test_every_rewrite_takes_a_slot.py::test_every_rewrite_call_passes_the_bound_FROM_SETTINGS\n- services/maintenance/tests/test_the_credential_tier_is_counted_not_only_logged.py::test_both_credential_paths_are_counted\n- services/maintenance/tests/test_the_drain_this_service_claims_is_actually_armed.py::test_the_service_arms_the_drain_it_documents\n- services/maintenance/tests/test_the_drain_this_service_claims_is_actually_armed.py::test_EVERY_subscription_lane_checks_the_retirement_budget\n- tests/unit/test_base_refs_guard.py::test_the_whole_estate_prepass_threads_the_SERVICE_session\n- services/ingest/tests/test_activity_inputs_are_coerced.py::test_every_activity_coerces_its_payload_before_using_it\n- services/ingest/tests/test_run_deadline.py::test_the_ceiling_refuses_BEFORE_any_unit_is_published\n- services/ingest/tests/test_staging_signs_with_the_vended_credential.py::test_every_ledger_CALL_SITE_hands_over_the_credential\n- services/ingest/tests/test_the_chunk_carries_the_table_identity.py::test_the_dispatcher_fills_it_from_the_ONE_place_that_derives_it\n- tests/unit/test_invariants.py::test_every_pod_whose_app_fails_closed_on_the_app_token_is_given_one\n  (its render half is sound; its subject set was built by grepping services/ for a call)\n\nSeveral of these readers were the only check on a real rule, and those rules now have no test: the\ncan_promote rung on an accept_assertions publish, revoke-before-drop on a warehouse cascade, the\ndescribe door''s base scope, the drain gate on POST /produce, the BYO-engine env contract between\nWorkOrder.to_env() and the stage jobs, watchers/push on the notifications bus lane, the app token\nfor pods that fail closed, and the max_units ceiling coming before any child workflow. Each needs a\nbehavioural test in its own row, through the owner.\n\nKept after reading, though flagged as candidates: test_the_tuple_tools_use_the_model_their_code_carries\n::test_the_carried_model_is_the_checkouts_body_in_the_estates_store, because its superset runs the\nmigration in a subprocess and deleting it lost write_model.py:96-105 from the union (measured, then\nrestored). test_history_limit_bound::test_the_limit_has_a_real_ceiling and\ntest_access_admin::test_every_access_route_is_covered_by_that_gate, because they inspect runtime route\nobjects, not source, and are the only pin of their bound and gate. The Cypher-constant checks in\ntest_a_branch_write_names_its_ref, test_a_catalog_drop_is_recognised_as_a_drop and the two lineage\nretention files, because they read production string values, not source files. That is the owner''s\ncall. Every chart-render test in scope was read and kept: none duplicates another''s render inputs and\nasserts.\n\nProse that named the deleted files was rewritten: scripts/ray_stage_job.py,\ntests/unit/test_ray_stage_job.py, services/ingest/tests/test_terminated_is_not_a_failure.py, the\nwarehouse-cascade module docstring, and the B6 row of docs/architecture/batch-processing-invariants.md.\nHelpers and imports orphaned by the deletions were removed.\n\nDefault lane (-m \"not slow and not e2e\" -n 8): 6070 passed, 5 skipped, 1 xfailed (6076 collected,\nfrom 6122).\n\ntests: +0 −46\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"3065bbe18f2a9d5081cc5950f076341150c69ed8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/3065bbe18f2a9d5081cc5950f076341150c69ed8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/f0c997f983e9c88066f61f448f3475954a454ac2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"h