minio:lakehouse-5b9f199e (sha256:f4170afb...) for the store and its scoped-users hook, every\nother stem unchanged. Health at 06:30:26Z, 15 min after the rollout: DLQ unchanged (ingest 1,\nlineage 1, both from before), no pod unready or restarted.\n\nxc075_live_probe.py: rev 289 deployed; rask-minio-0 runs localhost:5000/minio:lakehouse-5b9f199e\nwith the pushed digest and is ready; the r289 scoped-users hook succeeded on the same image;\nthe server still reports RELEASE.2025-04-22T22-12-26Z, commit 0d7408fc; no pod names an upstream\nminio image. That last check first failed on 19 finished pods of old hook Jobs (r146-r163, r288,\nrotate-scoped-users) still naming minio/mc; with the owner''s approval the 19 Jobs were deleted\n(they also carried credential literals, part of XC-004) and the check passed. The node pulled the\nestate image fresh during the upgrade; an upgrade on a node empty of every image waits on XC-096\nand is parked under LH-427.\n\nRegister: 191 open / 183 workable / 31 HIGH; short list 6 open with 24 enablers. Parked: LH-427.\nLive pins: minio lakehouse-5b9f199e.\n\ntests: +0 −0\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"388bf918b72c9e2dea958c48f2db185d8e69be35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/388bf918b72c9e2dea958c48f2db185d8e69be35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/a4ae551e56f968471ab8a0017cad5c2d956a5a2d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/a4ae551e56f968471ab8a0017cad5c2d956a5a2d","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKGE0YWU1NTFlNTZmOTY4NDcxYWI4YTAwMTdjYWQ1YzJkOTU2YTVhMmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/5b9f199ef3b156eb5ad4cc0290c8d46851f1d534","sha":"5b9f199ef3b156eb5ad4cc0290c8d46851f1d534","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/5b9f199ef3b156eb5ad4cc0290c8d46851f1d534"}],"sha":"a4ae551e56f968471ab8a0017cad5c2d956a5a2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/a4ae551e56f968471ab8a0017cad5c2d956a5a2d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/5b9f199ef3b156eb5ad4cc0290c8d46851f1d534/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T20:57:41Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T06:08:35Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"fix(chart): the object store and its scoped-users hook run a MinIO the estate builds from pinned source (XC-075)\n\nminio/minio and minio/mc refuse anonymous pulls on Docker Hub and quay.io\n(401 on the manifest, re-measured 2026-10-05), so a node with an empty\nimage cache could neither start rask-minio nor run the pre-upgrade\nminio-scoped-users hook. Owner decision D10: build MinIO with Dagger.\n\n- .docker/minio.dockerfile compiles the server at upstream tag\n  RELEASE.2025-04-22T22-12-26Z (commit 0d7408fc, the version rask-minio\n  runs) and mc at RELEASE.2025-08-13T08-35-41Z (commit 7394ce0d) with\n  upstream''s own ldflags; the build refuses a tag that no longer names its\n  recorded commit. One image carries both binaries, the layout upstream''s\n  release image used. Built through the existing seam:\n  `dagger call image --name=minio`. Default user stays root, as upstream''s\n  was and as the live pod runs, because the live data is uid-0-owned.\n- The chart renders both the StatefulSet and the hook''s mc container from\n  component `minio` through `rask.image` (registry, tag, per-component\n  digest), with the estate''s pull secrets. `minio.image` and\n  `minio.mcImage` are gone. The hook''s derive init container and data-base\n  seeding are unchanged.\n- The MinIO and mc services leave .docker/docker-compose.yml; the\n  docker-compose.rustfs.yml overlay (replaced by `dagger call\n  rustfs-lifecycle`) and docker-compose.local.yml (which only remapped the\n  MinIO ports) are deleted.\n- make k3s-build/k3s-import build and side-load `minio`; the kind e2e\n  lanes pick it up from the render through scripts/side_loaded_images.py.\n- scripts/k3s-pins.sh classifies a reference as first-party only when it is\n  bare or under localhost/172.*. It read the Docker Hub short form\n  `minio/minio:RELEASE...` as first-party (no dot in the head) and pinned\n  `image.tags.minio` to upstream''s RELEASE tag, which `rask.image` now\n  reads: a k3s-up would render localhost:5000/minio:RELEASE..., an image\n  nobody pushes, and fail the pre-upgrade hook. chart/values-live-pins.yaml\n  drops the ten third-party keys the corrected classifier no longer emits\n  (age, alertmanager, dashboard, minio, nats-box,\n  nats-server-config-reloader, openbao, openfga,\n  opentelemetry-collector-contrib, vmalert); its first-party tags are\n  unchanged. The first roll is `make k3s-converge STEM=minio TAG=<tag>`,\n  whose --set overrides the stored live key.\n\nMc stays rather than moving the hook to packages/storage: the hook drives\nthe MinIO admin API (users, policies), which no estate S3 seam speaks, so\nremoving mc is XC-083/XC-084''s work, not a precondition for this row.\n\nMeasured: every third-party image the chart (local + observability\nrenders), .dagger/*.go and the compose files name resolves anonymously.\nRelease size: +520 bytes on the Python-packed client render (projected\n1,031,228 of 1,048,576 against rev 285''s 1,030,708).\n\ntests: +1 -0. test_the_object_store_runs_an_image_the_estate_builds.py\npins the render (both pods on the estate''s registry, one digest reaching\nboth); red with the template change reverted. The existing\ntest_a_converged_estate_passes_and_says_so gains one case (an upstream\nminio/minio pod beside the estate''s localhost:5000/minio); red with the\nclassifier reverted (refused as a split `minio` stem). No test pinned\nminio''s image before. Subset-twin check (--cov --cov-context=test over\nthese two files and test_a_stack_builds_every_image_it_side_loads.py):\nunion of executed production lines 0 before and after, because a chart\nrender and the script''s inline Python run no covered production line,\nso no test is a subset twin and none is deleted.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"5c5e4809510b3b72732ac52a7ef881c1390c8ef9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/5c5e4809510b3b72732ac52a7ef881c1390c8ef9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/5b9f199ef3b156eb5ad4cc0290c8d46851f1d534","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/5b9f199ef3b156eb5ad4cc0290c8d46851f1d534","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKDViOWYxOTllZjNiMTU2ZWI1YWQ0Y2MwMjkwYzhkNDY4NTFmMWQ1MzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/6f04054152f160771931c28777cdcf04077c157d","sha":"6f04054152f160771931c28777cdcf04077c157d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/6f04054152f160771931c28777cdcf04077c157d"}],"sha":"5b9f199ef3b156eb5ad4cc0290c8d46851f1d534","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/5b9f199ef3b156eb5ad4cc0290c8d46851f1d534"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/6f04054152f160771931c28777cdcf04077c157d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T06:07:53Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T06:07:53Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"chore(estate): XC-077 and LH-247 close at helm rev 288; CP-056 step 2 is live\n\nRev 288, deployed from a build worktree at fdc53bd0 with every image built there:\nlance-rest-catalog, compute, controlplane, flows, ingest and notifications at lakehouse-fdc53bd0,\nray-cluster at lakehouse-68d4ca3c. Health at 06:07:13Z, 15 min after the rollout: DLQ unchanged\n(ingest 1, lineage 1, both from before), no pod unready or restarted.\n\nRev 286 (2026-10-05) rendered main''s chart, which already held XC-077, over images built at\n68d4ca3c without its code; the new OpenFGA pod and the issuer mirror crash-looped while the old\nOpenFGA pod kept serving (maxUnavailable 0), and rev 287''s restore could not remove OpenFGA\nsettings a failed revision had applied. Rev 288 is the intended end state.\n\n- XC-077 (f3c6146b), probe_openfga_authn.py: OpenFGA runs authn oidc, audience rask-openfga,\n  playground off; no bearer 401, wrong audience 401, a token from htr-batch:default 401, a non-\n  client rask SA 401, an rask-openfga client token 200; port 3000 refused; the mirror serves\n  discovery with its own jwks_uri; all 16 FGA client containers pass a Check through their own\n  build_fga_client with no refusal in their logs, each on its helm tag built from a tree carrying\n  XC-077.\n- LH-247 (fdc53bd0), lh247_live_probe.py (run 2; run 1''s namespace create lacked a warehouse, a\n  probe defect): /query k=0, above the ceiling and analyze_plan k=0 answer 400 code 13; a bounded\n  vector query serves 2048 rows; the change feed serves 40,000 rows; the catalog''s cgroup\n  memory.peak 339,243,008 bytes, under 512Mi, no restart, no OOMKilled.\n- CP-056 step 2 (68d4ca3c), cp056_step2_readback.py: a /produce ran through both Ray hops; each\n  handed off through the outcome door with committed_version equal to the job''s reported version\n  and tier_write_landed. CP-056 stays open for steps 3 and 4.\n\nRegister: 192 open / 184 workable / 32 HIGH; short list 7 open with 24 enablers. Parked: LH-425,\nLH-426. Live pins: the six stems at lakehouse-fdc53bd0, ray-cluster lakehouse-68d4ca3c.\n\ntests: +0 −0\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"76c4cd9c817df548d13d141eda1aafe6387f20d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/76c4cd9c817df548d13d141eda1aafe6387f20d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/6f04054152f160771931c28777cdcf04077c157d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/6f04054152f160771931c28777cdcf04077c157d","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKDZmMDQwNTQxNTJmMTYwNzcxOTMxYzI4Nzc3Y2RjZjA0MDc3YzE1N2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/fdc53bd02055b1782414b1c96a8f32c68eb53410","sha":"fdc53bd02055b1782414b1c96a8f32c68eb53410","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/fdc53bd02055b1782414b1c96a8f32c68eb53410"}],"sha":"6f04054152f160771931c28777cdcf04077c157d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/6f04054152f160771931c28777cdcf04077c157d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/fdc53bd02055b1782414b1c96a8f32c68eb53410/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T19:46:11Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T20:30:43Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"fix(catalog): Lance calls inside the catalog are bounded in time and memory, and a silent store answers 503 (LH-247)\n\nA wide change feed took the catalog past its 512Mi limit, a k=0 query answered\nevery row in one buffer, and a store that stopped answering held a worker for\nminutes and came back as a 404 or a 500. Each now has a bound that travels with\nthe code.\n\nTime, in two planes (CatalogReadBounds, service_kit.lakehouse.objectfs.StoreTimeouts).\nobject_store''s request timeout covers the whole request, body included, so one\nbudget cannot serve a manifest read and a 5 MiB upload part.\n- Metadata plane (LANCE_STORE_*: connect 2 s, request 5 s, no client retry): the\n  native namespace connection, so every describe/list/declare, which is also\n  the first store call every data door makes. One open against a store dropping\n  packets took 124.9 s on object_store''s defaults and 14.5 s on these; against\n  one that accepts and never answers, over 300 s and 32.8 s.\n- Data plane (same connect bound; LANCE_DATA_STORE_*: request 120 s, 3 retries,\n  300 s window): the pylance handles doors read and write through\n  (StorageOptionsDep) and a data twin of the native connection\n  (DataNamespaceDep) for /query, count_rows, analyze_plan, the native merge,\n  create_index, backfill and refresh. Through a proxy capping moto at 8 MB/s, a\n  100 MB write took 14.1 s and a 100 MB full read 13.3 s on these, and both\n  failed on the metadata plane''s.\nMeasured on pylance 12.0.0: object_store honours `timeout`, not the documented\n`request_timeout`; Lance re-issues a failed listing six times per open\nwhatever the client allows.\n\n503. service_kit.lancekit.outage.reads_as_store_outage recognises a store that\ndid not answer (pylance''s LanceError(IO) text, including a body cut off\nmid-transfer, and the native backend''s InternalError carrying a\nDebug-formatted IO error); install_problem_handlers answers it 503 code 17. A\n4xx from the store keeps its status. The catalog''s open no longer reads an\noutage as \"table not found\", and the change window''s walk no longer refuses\none as unfollowable.\n\nMemory. The lifespan sets Lance''s process scan defaults (IO buffer 32 MiB,\nbatch 1,024 rows, fragment readahead 1; LANCE_SCAN_IO_BUFFER_MB,\nLANCE_SCAN_BATCH_ROWS) unless the operator set Lance''s own variables: the one\nlever reaching the native backend''s scans and the change feed alike.\nLANCE_DEFAULT_BATCH_SIZE and LANCE_DEFAULT_FRAGMENT_READAHEAD are not in\nlance_docs/ or pylance''s docstrings; they are named in the 12.0.0 binary and\nmeasured. /query and analyze_plan refuse k=0, k or offset above u32, and k\nabove LANCE_QUERY_MAX_RESPONSE_MB of projected rows (400 code 13). offset is not\ncapped: the rows it skips are streamed past (k=1000 offset=39000 peaked at\n395,256 kB beside 381,412 kB for k=4000).\n\nConsumer moved: service_kit.lancekit.reader.CatalogTableReader (the\nannotator''s catalog-mode reader) sent k=1,000,000,000 for an unlimited read. It\nnow pages with a bounded k plus an offset, pinned to one version: 64 rows,\nthen 4 MiB of rows at the width the previous page measured, until a short page.\n\nMeasured from outside a one-CPU catalog under uvicorn over moto, 164 MB table\nof 1024-dim float32 vectors, limit 524,288 kB, Lance defaults -> bounds:\nchange feed 640,196 -> 354,012 kB; largest /query served (unindexed vector\nsearch) 628,000 -> 434,152 kB; k=0 822,192 kB -> refused.\n\nNot done here: the window walk still makes one read_transaction per version\nwith no count bound (parked LH-418).\n\ntests: +5 -2\n  + tests/integration/test_a_black_holed_store_answers_503_within_its_deadline.py (black hole -> 503; slow store still moves 16 MB)\n  + tests/integration/test_a_query_answer_is_bounded_before_it_is_read.py\n  + tests/integration/test_a_wide_read_stays_under_the_catalog_memory_limit.py\n  + tests/integration/test_a_catalog_reader_reads_a_whole_table_in_bounded_pages.py\n  - test_the_change_feed_answers_without_buffering_the_table.py::test_the_stream_survives_the_MIDDLEWARE_THE_SERVICE_ACTUALLY_SHIPS\n  - test_a_consumer_can_read_changes_since_a_version.py::test_the_feed_HANDS_OUT_its_answer_in_pieces_rather_than_holding_all_of_it\n  (both covered by the memory test, which measures the real app with its middleware)\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"6a5c4571682d22690a834c7fd7f919c338af981e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/6a5c4571682d22690a834c7fd7f919c338af981e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/fdc53bd02055b1782414b1c96a8f32c68eb53410","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/fdc53bd02055b1782414b1c96a8f32c68eb53410","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKGZkYzUzYmQwMjA1NWIxNzgyNDE0YjFjOTZhOGYzMmM2OGViNTM0MTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/f3c6146b95994090770177eafba62c754224d632","sha":"f3c6146b95994090770177eafba62c754224d632","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/f3c6146b95994090770177eafba62c754224d632"}],"sha":"fdc53bd02055b1782414b1c96a8f32c68eb53410","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/fdc53bd02055b1782414b1c96a8f32c68eb53410"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/f3c6146b95994090770177eafba62c754224d632/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T19:28:17Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T20:23:10Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"fix(openfga): OpenFGA admits only a projected token from a listed ServiceAccount, with no playground and no CORS origin (XC-077)\n\nThe deployed OpenFGA ran with no authn, the playground on and CORS `*`, so any pod, Ray workload code\nincluded, could write estate#admin for itself or replace the model with no rask audit record.\n\nOpenFGA now runs OIDC against the cluster ServiceAccount issuer with audience `rask-openfga` (D1, Lakekeeper''s\nmodel of an OpenFGA client authenticated by an OIDC provider, translated so the client holds no secret at all),\nand admits only the FGA clients'' accounts:\n\n- Subject allow-list: OPENFGA_AUTHN_OIDC_SUBJECTS comes from a ConfigMap rendered by `lance.openfgaSubjects`,\n  system:serviceaccount:<release namespace>:<sa> for exactly the pods that render `lance.fgaToken`. A pod in\n  another namespace, or an in-namespace non-client, is refused. Measured on openfga v1.18.3 through Dagger: a\n  comma-joined subjects env is split (both listed accounts admitted, unlisted refused), a space-joined one is\n  not. Env from a ConfigMap is read at start, so a new client needs an OpenFGA restart (fail closed).\n- service_kit: `fga.client_configuration` is the one builder; `provision`, `resolve`, `_named_store_id` and\n  `make_client` take a required `token_file` (RASK_FGA_TOKEN_FILE), presented through an SDK credential whose\n  `api_token` reads the file per request. A 401/403 at boot raises `OpenFgaCredentialRefusedError` from\n  `build_fga_client` whatever the service''s `fatal` posture, so a refused service crash-loops instead of\n  staying Ready with every door failing closed (maintenance keeps its never-raises contract and logs\n  `openfga_credential_refused`). `write_model` (the openfga-model hook) sends the token and exits 1 on 401/403.\n- chart: `lance.fgaToken` renders the env, projected volume and mount for catalog, lineage, controlplane,\n  compute, flows, ingest, notifications, maintenance (planner and worker), the medallion producer and stage\n  runners, the explorer trio and the bootstrap-admin and openfga-model Jobs. templates/openfga-authn.yaml\n  renders the subjects ConfigMap and the issuer mirror (`service_kit.governed.issuer_mirror`: OpenFGA fetches\n  discovery with no credential and k3s answers 401), and refuses a render whose audience, issuer alias or\n  subject source drifts. Playground off; CORS names one `.invalid` origin. The exclusive NetworkPolicy\n  ingress for OpenFGA waits on XC-009 and is not rendered.\n- Operator and e2e tooling present a token: in-pod tools read the pod''s, host tools (e2e_live, e2e_stack,\n  ray_e2e_stack, the medallion seed, demo and verify scripts, make notifications-lanes and its two .mjs\n  drives) mint a TokenRequest for <release>-sa-jobs.\n\nDEPLOY: rebuild and ship EVERY FGA-client image stem from this commit in the SAME revision as the chart:\nlance-rest-catalog (catalog, lineage, maintenance, medallion producer and stage runners, viewer, search,\nannotator, the bootstrap-admin and openfga-model Jobs, the issuer mirror), compute, controlplane, flows,\ningest, notifications. An image built before this commit sends no bearer and is refused 401 for good.\n\nRendered release on top of main: +7.4 KB packed (Python level-9 estimate on manifest + templates).\n\ntests: +6 −0\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"e75142413eb0f42dacea2431b9fc506badbcfd19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/e75142413eb0f42dacea2431b9fc506badbcfd19"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/f3c6146b95994090770177eafba62c754224d632","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/f3c6146b95994090770177eafba62c754224d632","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKGYzYzYxNDZiOTU5OTQwOTA3NzAxNzdlYWZiYTYyYzc1NDIyNGQ2MzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/68d4ca3ce9922101bca5af758b2822a35d9eb2e5","sha":"68d4ca3ce9922101bca5af758b2822a35d9eb2e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/68d4ca3ce9922101bca5af758b2822a35d9eb2e5"}],"sha":"f3c6146b95994090770177eafba62c754224d632","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/f3c6146b95994090770177eafba62c754224d632"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/68d4ca3ce9922101bca5af758b2822a35d9eb2e5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T19:32:05Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T20:20:58Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"refactor(medallion): both stage engines land their rows through one tier write, and both build their order with one builder (CP-056)\n\nCP-056 step 2. The in-process engine (compute.transform_stage) and the Ray stage job\n(scripts/ray_stage_job.py) each held their own write, and the Ray copy had drifted. New\nservice_kit.lakehouse.tier_write owns everything from produced rows to the run''s ONE marked\ncommit, and both engines import it (the Ray image ships service-kit[lancekit,media]):\n\n- plan_window: full or delta, decided before a row is read; a destination without stable row\n  ids is refused; a blob upstream converges whole.\n- write_tier, in commit order: disarm commit-path auto-cleanup (LH-245); delta lane retraction\n  from Lance''s deletion record (LH-216); widen by id (LH-213); declared dataset-id correction;\n  governance-label carry (LH-217); then ONE create (2.2, stable ids, the upstream''s external\n  base registered) or converge (merge_insert on id, full-sync on the full lane) carrying the\n  commit marker, re-planned on a retryable conflict. The lineage JSON index is built after the\n  marked commit, and the stage contract (cardinality, parentless rows) is checked last.\n- carried_blob_column: the upstream''s own blob field (thresholds, rask.classification) and the\n  values to write, external rows forwarded as pointers and managed rows carried as bytes.\n\nEach engine keeps only how it produces rows: the in-process table, and on Ray a driver table\n(head and delta), a re-runnable media stream, or a lance_ray staging dataset. ray_stage_job.py\ngoes from 1,059 to 436 lines; its _converge, _merge_into, _land_staged, _retract_deleted,\n_reset_if_legacy, _mergeable, _assert_stage_contract and per-batch media landing are deleted, as\nare compute''s widen, label-carry and index helpers.\n\nOne work-order builder: transform._work_order is deleted, and stage_submit.build_work_order\nbuilds the order for both lanes (build_stage_order wraps it with the Ray registration).\n\nDeliberate behaviour changes:\n- The in-process lane honours the trigger''s from_version (the order''s version_floor) and runs\n  the delta converge, checks the lane''s cardinality contract, and marks its last commit with\n  the run key.\n- The Ray lane forwards external blob pointers, keeps the upstream blob field, converges a\n  media run slice by slice ending on one marked commit (no run-id retraction), widens a tier by id, and\n  corrects a merged tier''s declared dataset id. This absorbs parked LH-326 (the Ray half of\n  LH-212, LH-216 and LH-217); LH-212''s conditioned merge now lands in one place.\n- Both lanes refuse a destination without stable row ids (the Ray lane''s directory wipe of\n  such a tier is deleted) and a full run that produced no rows from a non-empty upstream.\n- measure_stage no longer rebuilds the lineage index; the job builds it after its marked\n  commit, and the outcome''s committed version is the marked one.\n- The Ray job still signs with the head pod''s static S3 key; a run-bound write vend is LH-129.\n\nA streamed source converges in bounded memory. One whole-tier merge_insert over the media stream\npeaked at 1.29/3.43/6.05 GB VmHWM for 0.2/0.8/1.6 GB of 1 MiB blob rows (fresh process each,\npylance 12.0.0), and when_not_matched_by_source_delete reads every target payload even from an\nid-only source (0.65 GB into a 0.4 GB tier, 1.86 GB into 1.6 GB; a 16-row upsert stays 0.27 GB).\nSo each slice but the last lands as an unmarked upsert, the ids to retract are read from the\ntier''s id column and deleted by key, and the held-back last slice is the run''s one marked commit\n(an empty stream lands an empty marked upsert). A key repeated across slices is refused with\nLance''s ambiguous-merge message (LH-243). The media scans bound their read-ahead\n(io_buffer_size 64 MiB, one batch and one fragment of readahead; Lance''s default is 2 GB, and\nthe limit=0 schema probe alone peaked at 1.87 GB over 0.8 GB). Measured peaks, 128-row slices:\n1.18/1.78/2.06 GB at 0.2/0.8/1.6 GB (whole-tier merge 1.29/3.57/5.83; the previous job''s\nper-batch merges 1.26/1.82/2.76 as the reviewer measured). The residual growth is glibc keeping\none arena per host core: with MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=2 and ARROW_DEFAULT_MEMORY_POOL=system (the\nlakehouse pods'' lance.allocatorEnv) and 16-row slices the converge held 0.48/0.51 GB over\n256/800 MiB tiers against 1.23/2.74 GB for the whole-tier merge. The Ray head does not carry\nlance.allocatorEnv; that chart change is outside this step and is parked.\n\nWhere this makes CP-051 easier (not taken): write_tier already accepts a re-runnable\nRecordBatchReader factory, so the in-process engine can stream by handing it a factory instead\nof a materialised table; the contract and the empty-source guard count streamed rows.\n\nOne commit, not two: the builder dedupe is what lets the in-process lane reach the write''s\nwindow, contract and marker, so neither half is deployable or testable on its own.\n\nTests: tests/integration/test_both_engines_land_a_stage_through_one_write.py parametrizes the\nLH-216 (head refusal, delta window and retraction), LH-217 (blob payloads and field metadata),\nLH-213 (in-place correction, widen under a moving tier), LH-245 (armed tier) and CP-029 marker\nclaims over BOTH lanes, plus the media rerun ending on its marked commit, the null page, the\ndeclared id, the empty-source guard, and a memory proof of the streamed converge. It replaces test_stage_stamp_is_one_implementation.py,\ntest_the_stage_edge_names_the_data_version_not_the_index.py,\ntest_a_stage_rerun_carries_what_its_upstream_holds_now.py, 22 of tests/unit/test_ray_stage_job.py''s\n30 tests, and the moved cases in test_provenance_survives_a_re_seed.py,\ntest_the_stage_runner_forwards_pointers.py and test_blob_null_alignment.py. The five contract\nunits become one parametrized test on tier_write.assert_stage_contract.\ntests: +12 -42\n\nDeploy note: the lakehouse image and the ray-cluster image ship in ONE helm revision. A new stage\nrunner no longer builds the lineage index the old Ray job left to it, and the new job reports the\nmarked version. Live readback: POST /produce on the events chain; each Ray hop\n(bronze-to-silver, silver-to-gold) hands off with source=job and a committed_version equal to the\nversion= of its job''s RAY-STAGE OK line, the job logs tier_write_landed, and gold''s COMPLETE lands.\nEvery live lane runs on Ray, so the in-process leg needs a lane declared onto an inprocess task.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"67d7ec5c8a69350e2fd3addb1ff5a718273d2801","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/67d7ec5c8a69350e2fd3addb1ff5a718273d2801"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/68d4ca3ce9922101bca5af758b2822a35d9eb2e5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4867