ived_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/5a91a3c1336249c017ca56ec7c699e2426777e7b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T20:12:55Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T20:12:55Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"docs(register): owner rulings 2026-10-05: D10 builds MinIO with Dagger, ESO is a prerequisite\n\nD10 leaves the open decisions: the dev MinIO image is built by Dagger from a pinned upstream source\ntag (XC-075). XC-004''s closes-when now reads that ESO is a documented prerequisite and a render or\nmake k3s-up without it fails clearly; rask never installs ESO (R1). The day''s other rulings (CP-056,\nthe named-offline-proof closes) are listed with them.\n\ntests: +0 −0\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"aac9690313d90e1e2a1d8f06a537c5dbacf9d771","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/aac9690313d90e1e2a1d8f06a537c5dbacf9d771"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/5a91a3c1336249c017ca56ec7c699e2426777e7b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/5a91a3c1336249c017ca56ec7c699e2426777e7b","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKDVhOTFhM2MxMzM2MjQ5YzAxN2NhNTZlYzdjNjk5ZTI0MjY3NzdlN2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/c96d7e8cff80894e988502f0551335ce4bd5fdcc","sha":"c96d7e8cff80894e988502f0551335ce4bd5fdcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/c96d7e8cff80894e988502f0551335ce4bd5fdcc"}],"sha":"5a91a3c1336249c017ca56ec7c699e2426777e7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/5a91a3c1336249c017ca56ec7c699e2426777e7b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/c96d7e8cff80894e988502f0551335ce4bd5fdcc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T19:57:29Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T19:57:29Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"chore(estate): LH-273 and LH-252 close at helm rev 284, LH-243 at rev 285\n\nRev 284 (lance-rest-catalog lakehouse-e394ddbf; the chart now seeds the multibase fixture) and\nrev 285 (lakehouse-c6e1f231). Rev 284 first went to a tag whose build had died on an unreachable\nDagger engine; the engine was restarted, the image built under that tag, and the pre-upgrade hook\npulled it inside the release timeout. Read back: 12 running lakehouse pods on each revision''s tag.\nHealth at 19:39:03Z (rev 284) and 19:57:09Z (rev 285), 15 min after each rollout: DLQ unchanged\n(ingest 1, lineage 1, both from before), no pod unready or restarted.\n\n- Fixture (e394ddbf): minio-scoped-users r284 provisioned user lh067-second-store with policy\n  rask-base-lh067-second-store; OpenBao seeded secret/lh067-second-store (version 1, 19:23:00Z)\n  and carried every signing pair; the catalog''s lookup of it answers 200 (it answered 500).\n- LH-273 (5bc5314e, 232418b7): lh273_readrows.py, rule fixed before running: a table created on\n  s3://lh067-second-store/data answers /changes begin 0 inserted with exactly ids [1, 2, 3].\n  The rule''s per-table-directory half was not asserted by the script and is not claimed here.\n  232418b7 makes an unresolvable base credential answer a typed 503 in seconds.\n- LH-252 (4ee229d9): lh252_live_probe.py leg V MEDIATED: two tables created on the real second\n  store, A''s vend answers server_mediated and issues no credential. Leg T (thief registration)\n  needs a static store key the probe does not have and was not run live. Closed on that plus the\n  named offline proof (owner ruling 2026-10-05): the sibling-policy case judged by moto''s IAM\n  evaluator and the thief-registration case in\n  services/catalog/tests/test_a_vend_for_one_table_grants_no_sibling_on_its_data_base.py.\n- LH-243 (c6e1f231): lh243_probe.py on a table whose id is the declared primary key: an insert\n  repeating a key within its rows and one repeating a held key each answer 400 code 13 with the\n  table unchanged; a new key answers 200; a fresh create carrying (5, 5) answers 400 and leaves\n  no table.\n\nRegister: 194 open / 186 workable / 33 HIGH; short list 9 open with 24 enablers. Parked: LH-423,\nLH-424. Live pins: lance-rest-catalog lakehouse-c6e1f231.\n\ntests: +0 −0\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"b5649f463b685e0b30cd58b32f8c0e9448504b76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/b5649f463b685e0b30cd58b32f8c0e9448504b76"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/c96d7e8cff80894e988502f0551335ce4bd5fdcc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/c96d7e8cff80894e988502f0551335ce4bd5fdcc","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKGM5NmQ3ZThjZmY4MDg5NGU5ODg1MDJmMDU1MTMzNWNlNGJkNWZkY2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/c6e1f2311bde4af6bef8d07b20bbc3e5f87ef1c4","sha":"c6e1f2311bde4af6bef8d07b20bbc3e5f87ef1c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/c6e1f2311bde4af6bef8d07b20bbc3e5f87ef1c4"}],"sha":"c96d7e8cff80894e988502f0551335ce4bd5fdcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/c96d7e8cff80894e988502f0551335ce4bd5fdcc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/c6e1f2311bde4af6bef8d07b20bbc3e5f87ef1c4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T19:10:35Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T19:28:59Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"fix(catalog): a write repeating a table''s primary key is refused at every door, and an ambiguous merge is held, not retried (LH-243)\n\nLance declares an unenforced primary key in field metadata and checks it on\nno write: measured on pylance 12.0.0, a create, an append and an unmatched\nmerge-insert all commit a repeated key, and the next merge whose source\nrepeats a key the target holds is refused \"Ambiguous merge inserts are\nprohibited\" forever. lance_docs/file_format.md:2887-2893 leaves enforcement\nto the writer.\n\nCatalog: catalog.services.primary_keys reads the table''s key through\nLanceSchema.unenforced_primary_key. Every door (/create fresh and\nOverwrite, /insert, /commit, /merge_insert) refuses rows repeating a key\namong themselves (pyarrow group_by). /insert appends to a keyed table\nthrough merge_insert(keys).when_matched_fail().when_not_matched_insert_all()\n.execute(): refused when the key is held as it lands, and re-planned on a\nlost race, so two inserts racing one new key land it once (20 of 20 races\nclean on 12.0.0, where check-then-append landed both every time). /commit\nreads the appended keys off its detached commit, selecting the fragments by\nthe op''s own data files (a compaction since read_version rewrites the\ntable''s rows into fragments new to the detached version too), and judges\nthem against the ref''s latest version through a key-only\nmerge_insert(keys).when_matched_fail() planned with execute_uncommitted,\nwhich writes nothing. Refusals are 400 InvalidInput (13) and leave the\ntable at its version. A table with no declared key is append-only by the\nformat''s definition and is not judged.\n\nMedallion: the in-process executor classifies Lance''s ambiguous-merge\nrefusal as RunFailure kind \"data\"; the stage raises RefusedByDataError and\nhandle_stage FAILs the run, holds it BLOCKED through _report_hold and acks\nquality_blocked instead of RETRY.\n\nBounds, measured on 12.0.0: a key nested in a struct is judged within the\nrows only (merge_insert cannot key on a nested field), and /commit''s\njudgement and its real commit are two steps: a writer landing the same new\nkey between them lands too (Append rebases over Append without comparing\nkeys, and an Append has no merge form).\n\ntests: +2 −0 (the catalog test carries 10 cases)\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"f0870ba545710f6c3acd37d56c355872b0f19959","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/f0870ba545710f6c3acd37d56c355872b0f19959"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/c6e1f2311bde4af6bef8d07b20bbc3e5f87ef1c4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/c6e1f2311bde4af6bef8d07b20bbc3e5f87ef1c4","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKGM2ZTFmMjMxMWJkZTRhZjZiZWY4ZDA3YjIwYmJjM2U1Zjg3ZWYxYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/e394ddbfcb642d98a9397f73d2825d952be9fd7e","sha":"e394ddbfcb642d98a9397f73d2825d952be9fd7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/e394ddbfcb642d98a9397f73d2825d952be9fd7e"}],"sha":"c6e1f2311bde4af6bef8d07b20bbc3e5f87ef1c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/c6e1f2311bde4af6bef8d07b20bbc3e5f87ef1c4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/e394ddbfcb642d98a9397f73d2825d952be9fd7e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:48:49Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:54:45Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"feat(chart): the local chart owns each data base''s scoped user and OpenBao entry (LH-273)\n\nEnabler of LH-273 and LH-252''s live proof. The live estate''s one per-base\ncredential reference, `lh067-second-store`, named an OpenBao entry and a\nMinIO user made by hand for LH-067 (4dd7faba records it); the entry is gone\nand Dapr answers 500 for it, so the per-base path cannot be proved.\n\n`catalog.multibase.devSeed` (false in values.yaml, true in values-local)\nmakes the chart own the fixture, per `baseCredentialRefs` reference:\n\n- minio-scoped-users: `mc mb --ignore-existing` for each base''s bucket, a\n  policy `rask-base-<ref>` reaching only that reference''s bases (bucket\n  metadata, LIST conditioned on `<prefix>` / `<prefix>/*`, object\n  read/write under `<prefix>/`), and a user `<ref>` holding it.\n- the dev OpenBao''s seed: `secret/<ref>` with `aws_access_key_id=<ref>` and\n  the secret under the field the catalog reads (new helper\n  `lance.catalogSecretField`, now also what the catalog Deployment renders),\n  the shape `warehouse_credentials.resolve` requires.\n\nThe secret is derived in the cluster, never rendered:\nsha256(\"<ref>-s3-<root>\")[:40], the `lance.scopedStorageSecret` function,\ncomputed by a `derive` init container (openbao image, root secret read as a\nmounted file, written to a memory emptyDir that mc reads) and by the seed,\nso the two halves agree without either handing the other a key, re-runs are\nidempotent and the seed''s re-seed loop restores the entry after an OpenBao\nrestart. No new env secret, no value in values. A real deployment, MinIO\noff or a non-dev OpenBao refuses the toggle at render.\n\nRelease size: +4,376 bytes packed (Python level 6 delta over the\nvalues-local render, templates and values).\n\ntests: +1 -0 (tests/unit/test_a_base_credential_ref_is_seeded_by_the_local_fixture.py)\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"162504a98a7a81f5361c8f19d0b8706b14ffb24f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/162504a98a7a81f5361c8f19d0b8706b14ffb24f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/e394ddbfcb642d98a9397f73d2825d952be9fd7e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/e394ddbfcb642d98a9397f73d2825d952be9fd7e","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKGUzOTRkZGJmY2I2NDJkOThhOTM5N2Y3M2QyODI1ZDk1MmJlOWZkN2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/ed0b3b24be20eeae6c908c2c01f244ee360e360c","sha":"ed0b3b24be20eeae6c908c2c01f244ee360e360c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/ed0b3b24be20eeae6c908c2c01f244ee360e360c"}],"sha":"e394ddbfcb642d98a9397f73d2825d952be9fd7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/e394ddbfcb642d98a9397f73d2825d952be9fd7e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/ed0b3b24be20eeae6c908c2c01f244ee360e360c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:48:51Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:48:51Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"chore(estate): CP-044 and LH-245 close at helm rev 283\n\nRev 283: lance-rest-catalog and ray-cluster both lakehouse-50a87b57 in one revision (CP-044''s\ndeploy condition; no training trigger pending on TRAINING beforehand: 1 message, acked).\nRead back: 12 running lakehouse pods on lakehouse-50a87b57, the Ray head on\nray-cluster:lakehouse-50a87b57, ingest unchanged on lakehouse-dea984c5. Health at 18:48:13Z,\n15 min after the rollout settled: DLQ unchanged (ingest 1, lineage 1, both from before), no pod\nunready or restarted.\n\n- CP-044 (90bfb6eb), cp044_train_probe.py: POST /train 202 with a 40-hex instance_id; the Ray job\n  under that submission id runs ray_train_job.py with only the RASK_* order names (no MODEL,\n  TRAIN_TOKEN or LINEAGE_URL, no empty value); the plan closed succeeded with outcome source \"job\"\n  and committed_version 108; Ray SUCCEEDED; lineage run COMPLETE.\n- LH-245 (50a87b57), lh245_refix_probe.py: a declare carrying lance.auto_cleanup.interval answers\n  400 code 13 and leaves nothing; a table armed out of band with a maintain vend keeps every\n  version across three insert-door appends (lost []), carries no key after the first append, and\n  keeps every version across an erasure with retain_days 30 (lost [], keys left []).\n\nLH-273 and LH-252 stay open: the live second store''s OpenBao entry, hand-made for LH-067, no\nlonger exists (Dapr 500 for lance-secrets/lh067-second-store, 200 for the catalog''s other keys).\n232418b7 makes such a request answer a typed 503 in seconds instead of holding a worker past 60 s;\nthe owner chose to have the chart seed the fixture (in progress), then the LH-252 probe runs.\n\nRegister: 197 open / 189 workable / 33 HIGH; short list 12 open with 24 enablers. Parked: LH-421,\nLH-422. Live pins: lance-rest-catalog and ray-cluster lakehouse-50a87b57.\n\ntests: +0 −0\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"2908303a12d09a6d0b1d8f80ac85794c51a1e9a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/2908303a12d09a6d0b1d8f80ac85794c51a1e9a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/ed0b3b24be20eeae6c908c2c01f244ee360e360c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/ed0b3b24be20eeae6c908c2c01f244ee360e360c","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKGVkMGIzYjI0YmUyMGVlYWU2YzkwOGMyYzAxZjI0NGVlMzYwZTM2MGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/232418b7facdc10bdf952921dd8997572b45e88b","sha":"232418b7facdc10bdf952921dd8997572b45e88b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/232418b7facdc10bdf952921dd8997572b45e88b"}],"sha":"ed0b3b24be20eeae6c908c2c01f244ee360e360c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/ed0b3b24be20eeae6c908c2c01f244ee360e360c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/232418b7facdc10bdf952921dd8997572b45e88b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:45:17Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:45:43Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"fix(catalog): a data base whose credential cannot be resolved fails the request in seconds, typed (LH-273)\n\nLH-273 resolves a data base''s credential reference on every open. On the\nlive estate the OpenBao entry behind s3://lh067-second-store/data''s\nreference is gone, Dapr answers 500, and the resolver ran the secret\nfetch''s BOOT policy (10 attempts, backoff to 15 s): catalog logs show waits\nof 12.4 s, 15 s, 15 s, ... from 18:35:19 to 18:36:16Z while the client timed\nout at 60 s with the worker still held.\n\n- fetch_required_secrets takes the fetch policy per call (timeout, retries,\n  backoff), defaulting to the boot policy, so every other secret and every\n  boot path is unchanged.\n- warehouse_credentials.resolve, the request-path resolver, passes two\n  1 s attempts with a 0.25 s backoff: a store that cannot answer fails the\n  open in about 2.5 s.\n- compose_base_store_params turns a failed resolution into\n  BaseCredentialUnavailableError (ServiceUnavailable, 503, retryable). A\n  5xx detail is redacted estate-wide, so the base, the reference and the\n  store ride as RFC 9457 extension members (data_base,\n  credential_reference, secret_store); never a secret value. Nothing falls\n  back to the estate key.\n- Every door that opens or writes such a table answers the same: the pylance\n  reads, the vend and describe(vend) through dataset_facts, and create and\n  overwrite through _write_blob.\n\nNot changed: resolve''s lru_cache does not cache a failure, so each request\non such a table spends the 2.5 s again until the secret exists.\n\ntests: +1 -1 (new: the two-store fixture with the sidecar answering 500,\nparametrized over a read, the vend and a create — 503 with the reference\nnamed, in under 6 s. Deleted: the unit case of compose re-raising a resolver\nfailure, which the new test covers end to end.)\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"3fd2960054bbe27a56d0e8add405edc65de59228","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/3fd2960054bbe27a56d0e8add405edc65de59228"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/232418b7facdc10bdf952921dd8997572b45e88b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/232418b7facdc10bdf952921dd8997572b45e88b","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKDIzMjQxOGI3ZmFjZGMxMGJkZjk1MjkyMWRkODk5NzU3MmI0NWU4OGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/50a87b572251279ce3d20ec0ef2c48e62acde301","sha":"50a87b572251279ce3d20ec0ef2c48e62acde301","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/50a87b572251279ce3d20ec0ef2c48e62acde301"}],"sha":"232418b7facdc10bdf952921dd8997572b45e88b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/232418b7facdc10bdf952921dd8997572b45e88b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/50a87b572251279ce3d20ec0ef2c48e62acde301/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:59:53Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:21:40Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"fix(catalog): every committing door and static-key lane disarms commit-path auto-cleanup, and no door can arm it (LH-245)\n\nThe sweep-only disarm (c620de1f) failed live on helm rev 280: the queue lane is hours behind (LH-195),\nso an armed table kept deleting versions on every ordinary commit until the sweep arrived; three appends\nthrough the insert door deleted versions 1 and 2.\n\nMeasured on pylance 12.0.0: Lance''s commit-path cleanup reads the config of the manifest a commit\nPRODUCES. A delete_config_keys that disarms deletes nothing, and an append through a handle opened\nbefore it (insert, or LanceDataset.commit of an Append at the stale read version) rebases onto the\ndisarmed manifest and deletes nothing. .interval alone arms; schema-metadata keys arm nothing; an\noverwrite carries the config forward; a restore produces the restored version''s config. pylance 12''s\nPython write_dataset/insert/merge_insert/commit take no skip_auto_cleanup (the native WriteParams field\nexists, write_dataset''s params dict never sets it).\n\n- service_kit.lakehouse.auto_cleanup: the prefix, armed_keys and disarm (writes only when a key is\n  present, since delete_config_keys commits even with nothing to delete). The maintenance sweep''s\n  disarm and write probe now use it; the sweep stays the backstop for a table nobody commits on.\n- core/namespace.disarm_commit_path_cleanup / open_dataset_for_commit / disarm_every_ref: every catalog\n  door that commits disarms the ref first: insert, merge_insert (both arms), update, delete,\n  add/alter/drop columns, field and schema metadata (both paths), /commit (main and branch),\n  /compaction_commit, create in overwrite mode, the merge-key index build, create_index,\n  create_scalar_index, drop_index, the in-pod compact and reindex doors, and the erasure door, which\n  disarms main and every branch head before its first delete: its deletes and compactions are commits,\n  and its retain_days window is the only reclamation it may do.\n- The restore door refuses (400 code 13) a version whose config carries the keys: the keys arrive\n  with the restore''s own commit, so no disarm can precede it.\n- core/formats: the property guard every create/declare/register/update/namespace door calls also\n  refuses lance.auto_cleanup.* (400 code 13); renamed reject_unsupported_properties.\n- The static-key writers outside the catalog disarm before their first commit on a tier, without\n  restructuring them (CP-056): medallion''s in-process lane (compute.open_to_commit for the seed merge,\n  the by-id widening merge, the full-sync merge, the label carry and the lineage index; the media\n  ingest''s overwrite of an existing bronze) and scripts/ray_stage_job.py (_disarm_destination, once\n  per run, before any merge, retraction delete or write).\n\nNot covered: the Ray job''s staging dataset is created by overwrite and not disarmed; alter_transaction\nwas not probed and does not disarm.\n\ntests: +1 -1 (+1 test_an_ordinary_append_never_deletes_a_version.py, parametrized over /insert, /commit\nand /erasure, replacing the sweep-tick append test in test_no_commit_but_the_sweeps_reclaims_a_version.py;\nan armed-tier case on test_a_stage_rerun_carries_what_its_upstream_holds_now.py''s in-place-correction\ntest and on test_ray_stage_job.py''s delta-run test; one case added to test_format_guard.py''s existing\nrefusal test; four door-test fakes gain the config() the door now calls, and test_api''s restore test\npatches the unchecked open it now makes)\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"a6456b9498c85458d50d43559b2bfef9b001dfdf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/a6456b9498c85458d50d43559b2bfef9b001dfdf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/50a87b572251279ce3d20ec0ef2c48e62acde301","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/50a87b572251279ce3d20ec0ef2c48e62acde301","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKDUwYTg3YjU3MjI1MTI3OWNlM2QyMGVjMGVmMmM0OGU2MmFjZGUzMDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/4ee229d92ed187b366744f8d9e217939b2ca4a5c","sha":"4ee229d92ed187b366744f8d9e217939b2ca4a5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/4ee229d92ed187b366744f8d9e217939b2ca4a5c"}],"sha":"50a87b572251279ce3d20ec0ef2c48e62acde301","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/50a87b572251279ce3d20ec0ef2c48e62acde301"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/4ee229d92ed187b366744f8d9e217939b2ca4a5c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:38:23Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:19:02Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"fix(catalog): a table on a data base registers its own directory, and a vend grants only that (LH-252)\n\nEvery table naming an approved data base registered the base itself, so\nall of their fragments round-robined into one flat <base>/ and the STS\nsession policy vended for any one of them granted READ on <base>/* —\nevery sibling''s fragments for the credential''s lifetime.\n\n- A create mints one directory per table and registers\n  <approved base>/<directory> (dataplane.table_data_bases); the base record\n  and the manifest name the same path. The target name stays derived from\n  the approved base, so a re-sent data_base on an overwrite resolves to the\n  directory the manifest registered (dataplane.registered_data_bases), and\n  an approved base the table never registered is refused 400 instead of\n  reaching pylance as an unknown target. Measured on pylance 12.0.0:\n  DatasetBasePath(<base>/<dir>, is_dataset_root=False) writes its fragments\n  under <dir>/ and reads them back.\n- build_session_policy grants an allowlisted data base only as a directory\n  strictly beneath an allowlist entry; a manifest declaring the approved\n  base itself is granted nothing.\n- A table''s data directory is HELD by it: each directory is claimed\n  put-if-not-exists through service_kit.lakehouse.location_claims (LH-204''s\n  shape, beside the table-location claims under _locations/). The create\n  door takes the claim before the base record; the register door admits a\n  data base only as ONE directory beneath an approved base (the shape a\n  create mints, so overlap is equality) and refuses 400 a directory another\n  live table holds; forget_base_record releases the table''s directory claims\n  with its record, so the destructive drop, the namespace cascade, the\n  warehouse trash clear and the maintenance purge all free them. Without the\n  claim a registration declaring another table''s directory was admitted and\n  vended GET on that table''s fragments.\n\nExisting flat-base tables are test data: a vend no longer grants their\nfragments.\n\nCloses-when needs the deployed MinIO STS. The offline pin drives the real\ncreate, register and credentials doors with the lifespan-built StsVendor,\non an approved data base with no credential reference (one with a reference\nis never vended directly, LH-273), and judges the policy it hands to\nAssumeRole with moto''s IAM evaluator against the object keys each table''s\nfragments occupy; the live probe for the deployed estate is handed over\nseparately.\n\ntests: +1 -1 (new: the two-table test, parametrized over a created sibling''s\nvend and a registration over the owner''s directory. Deleted:\nthe factory-wiring unit test, which the new test''s control assertion covers.\nThe flat-base policy case is rewritten to the per-table shape; the multibase\nunit tests and the planted-base fixture move to the DataBase API.)\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"a39e35d7aeac0aaaa2bc720fc9a25f7f858b6ac4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/a39e35d7aeac0aaaa2bc720fc9a25f7f858b6ac4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/4ee229d92ed187b366744f8d9e217939b2ca4a5c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/4ee229d92ed187b366744f8d9e217939b2ca4a5c","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKDRlZTIyOWQ5MmVkMTg3YjM2Njc0NGY4ZDllMjE3OTM5YjJjYTRhNWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/5bc5314e6eaf7538a112541652239048ccc0f398","sha":"5bc5314e6eaf7538a112541652239048ccc0f398","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/5bc5314e6eaf7538a112541652239048ccc0f398"}],"sha":"4ee229d92ed187b366744f8d9e217939b2ca4a5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/4ee229d92ed187b366744f8d9e217939b2ca4a5c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/5bc5314e6eaf7538a112541652239048ccc0f398/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:23:55Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:19:02Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"fix(catalog): every open of a multi-base table carries each base''s own credential (LH-273)\n\nA table whose fragments sit on a data base under its own credential was\nwritten with that base''s base_store_params and read with the estate''s\noptions only, so a read sent the estate key to the second store. Measured\non pylance 12.0.0 over a moto server enforcing per-key bucket policies: the\nread fails \"lacked the necessary privileges\", and the map''s key must be the\nmanifest''s exact base path (a trailing slash or the parent is not matched).\n\n- core/namespace.open_location opens, composes base_store_params from the\n  manifest''s base paths and the credential references, and reopens with\n  them on the shared session; a branch is checked out from that handle and\n  composed from the branch manifest. open_dataset, open_dataset_unchecked,\n  vending.dataset_facts and vending.table_has_branch all open through it.\n- The references ride the installed BaseJudge (BaseCredentials), the same\n  deployment configuration the bases are judged against.\n- judged_native_version refuses (406 UnsupportedOperation) a table with a\n  base under its own credential: the native DirectoryNamespace open takes no\n  base_store_params and would read that base under the estate key.\n- The credentials door and describe(vend_credentials) answer\n  server_mediated for such a table: an STS credential is minted from the\n  estate role, whose live MinIO policy reaches every bucket, so a direct\n  client would read the base under the estate identity.\n- Maintenance refuses a table whose data files live on a plain data base\n  outside its root (refused_by=foreign_data_base, counted by the existing\n  refusal counter, before any compaction, index or reclaim step). BOUNDARY:\n  maintenance holds no credential reference and no secret (the chart renders\n  LANCE_MULTIBASE_BASE_CREDENTIAL_REFS on the catalog alone), so it cannot\n  tell a referenced base from an unreferenced one and refuses every data\n  base fail-closed rather than touch one under its own key.\n- compose_base_store_params matches a declared base at or under a\n  configured base, ignores references for bases the table does not declare,\n  and strips every spelling of the estate key before adding the base''s pair:\n  the catalog''s options say access_key_id and the pair aws_access_key_id,\n  so an entry held two identities and the same write landed under either\n  key from run to run.\n- A reference for a base off LANCE_MULTIBASE_DATA_BASES is refused where\n  the map is parsed (Settings.multibase_base_credential_ref_map).\n- The write path takes one BaseCredentials instead of three parameters.\n- The false comments in dataplane._write_blob and core/config.py are\n  rewritten.\n- tests/e2e-py/test_multibase_e2e.py compares the rows read with the rows\n  written instead of counting them.\n\nNot threaded: medallion and service-kit reads. Neither holds a credential\nreference, and the medallion cascade is single-base by design.\n\ntests: +2 -3 (new: the two-store read test, parametrized over a pylance\ndoor, an overwrite, a native door and the vend; the off-allowlist reference\ncase moved into the config test. The maintenance gate test drives the real\nunit path over a mixed table and a data-base table instead of calling the\ncounter directly; the base-resident compaction test names the new gate. Deleted: the unit case composing a referenced base, now covered end to\nend; the unregistered-reference case, moved; the AST reader of dataplane.py.)\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"4d1d46554a196d1f19b21827081db0d42ae88ab2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/4d1d46554a196d1f19b21827081db0d42ae88ab2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/5bc5314e6eaf7538a112541652239048ccc0f398","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/5bc5314e6eaf7538a112541652239048ccc0f398","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKDViYzUzMTRlNmVhZjc1MzhhMTEyNTQxNjUyMjM5MDQ4Y2NjMGYzOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/90bfb6eba8da3a592df6d6e91b5eba9edcbba9b9","sha":"90bfb6eba8da3a592df6d6e91b5eba9edcbba9b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/90bfb6eba8da3a592df6d6e91b5eba9edcbba9b9"}],"sha":"5bc5314e6eaf7538a112541652239048ccc0f398","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/5bc5314e6eaf7538a112541652239048ccc0f398"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/90bfb6eba8da3a592df6d6e91b5eba9edcbba9b9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:04:29Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:17:27Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"refactor(medallion): training submits a WorkOrder through the port, and the resubmit reads DURABLE_RECORD (CP-044)\n\nStep 1 of the reviewed CP-056 plan. No transport change: the Ray adapter is\nstill in medallion.\n\n- The stage sweep resubmits a lost run only when the executor withholds\n  Capability.DURABLE_RECORD; behind an engine that claims it, a lost record\n  closes the run failed at once. The Ray adapter withholds it, so the Ray\n  lane is unchanged.\n- Training is a WorkOrder (train_plans.train_order) submitted through\n  executor_for(plan.engine). WorkOrder.source is optional, a new\n  replace_failed_run (default True) picks the adapter''s terminal-failure\n  policy, and to_env emits RASK_TOKEN. SubmitOutcome.ALREADY_FAILED and a\n  port EngineError (RayJobError subclasses it) join executor.py; the train\n  consumer retries on EngineError. The run key is derive_idempotency_key\n  over the token and registry URI (train_plans.train_action_id), and\n  POST /train answers it as instance_id so a caller can poll /trains/<id>.\n- submit_train_job, train_submission_id and ray_jobs_api.submission_id are\n  deleted. ray_submit.py keeps only the adapter''s pooled client; planners\n  close it through engine_registry.close_executors.\n- scripts/ray_train_job.py reads the order''s names (RASK_PARAM_MODEL,\n  RASK_TOKEN, RASK_PARAM_FEATURES, RASK_PARAM_CONFIG,\n  RASK_PARAM_ARTIFACT_BASE, RASK_DEST_URI, RASK_STAGE, RASK_ORIGINATOR,\n  RASK_PROJECT) and takes the lineage endpoint from the pod''s\n  RASK_LINEAGE_ENDPOINT. lineage-kit drops the LINEAGE_URL alias nothing\n  sends any more.\n- Deviation from the plan: MEDALLION_TRAIN_LINEAGE_URL is kept. The job no\n  longer receives it, but cascade_lag_readers reads it as the producer''s\n  lineage address; renaming it is a chart change and waits for CP-056.\n- Contract: only-the-ray-adapter-speaks-the-jobs-api (type protected)\n  replaces the-workflow-reads-ray-through-the-port. A forbidden contract\n  with medallion as source cannot fail on its own descendants (measured on\n  import-linter 2.15). Mutation-checked: an added ray_submit import in\n  train_plans broke it; removed, 9 kept.\n- Prose: medallion pyproject, DECISIONS.md (adapter paragraph, the\n  2026-09-17 heading, a CP-044 entry), RAY-TRAIN.md D2, the\n  stage_submission_id comments in work_order, rayjobs_api_executor,\n  bronze_arrival and control_relay.\n\nDeploy note: lance-rest-catalog and ray-cluster ship in ONE helm revision.\nThe job script now reads RASK_PARAM_MODEL and RASK_TOKEN and the submission\nsends only those, so an old head under a new producer (or the reverse) dies\non a KeyError before its lineage FAIL and only the sweep closes the run.\nDeploy while no training trigger is pending: an old pod that planned under\nray-train-<token> and did not ack (SIGTERM, or RETRY while the head restarts\nin the same revision) is redelivered to a new pod that plans a second run\nunder the new key, and the originator then hears both failed and succeeded.\nA plan already open keeps its old id and the sweep resolves it as before.\n\ntests: +1 -18\n(+1 durable-record case of the stage resubmit test; -10 test_submission_id,\n-3 submit_train_job transport tests, -1 originator link merged, -1 train arm\nestatewide, -1 train arm medallion no-secret, -2 source-reader tests;\nthe training keeper now runs the job on the env its submission carried.)\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"b7dcc04b53e9c7ce1b5bbba2e2d260a655c79c35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/b7dcc04b53e9c7ce1b5bbba2e2d260a655c79c35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/90bfb6eba8da3a592df6d6e91b5eba9edcbba9b9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/90bfb6eba8da3a592df6d6e91b5eba9edcbba9b9","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKDkwYmZiNmViYThkYTNhNTkyZGY2ZDZlOTFiNWViYTllZGNiYmE5Yjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/06faba82fc9b6cd6591e2992ba549f31c74d07d8","sha":"06faba82fc9b6cd6591e2992ba549f31c74d07d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/06faba82fc9b6cd6591e2992ba549f31c74d07d8"}],"sha":"90bfb6eba8da3a592df6d6e91b5eba9edcbba9b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/90bfb6eba8da3a592df6d6e91b5eba9edcbba9b9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/06faba82fc9b6cd6591e2992ba549f31c74d07d8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:16:26Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:16:26Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"chore(estate): LH-194, LH-216, LH-241 and LH-202 close at helm revs 281 and 282\n\nRev 281 (lance-rest-catalog lakehouse-dea984c5 on every lakehouse deployment) and rev 282\n(ingest lakehouse-dea984c5, since LH-202 and the shared kit changed ingest''s code). Read back:\nall 13 running lakehouse pods on lakehouse-dea984c5, ingest on ingest:lakehouse-dea984c5.\nHealth at 18:15:46Z, 15 min after rev 282 settled: DLQ unchanged (ingest 1, lineage 1, both from\nbefore), no pod unready or restarted.\n\n- LH-202 (dea984c5), live against MinIO STS (lh202_live_probe.py, runs 1 and 2): under the write\n  vend, commits of DataReplacement, UpdateBases, Overwrite, Restore and a direct Append all fail at\n  the store writing _transactions/; puts to _refs/ (branch, tag), tree/, _mem_wal/ and a delete of\n  _versions/ are AccessDenied; the sibling prefix is refused at the write and maintain tiers;\n  write_fragments + /commit lands rows on main and on a branch (run 2, owner-level token for the\n  branch create); the maintain vend compacts (2 fragments to 1) and cleans up (3 versions); zero\n  maintenance denials. The four ''..'' legs answered XMinioInvalidResourceName where the rule as\n  written named XMinioInvalidObjectName (INCONCLUSIVE by the rule); a control with its rule fixed\n  before running shows the store refuses ''..'' keys under the whole-prefix maintain vend too, so no\n  ''..'' key can be stored or normalised.\n- LH-216 (9f66a9ea) and LH-241 (3dfdd758, fe0e40d5), b11_probe.py: a closed window answers the\n  same ids and row ids after the table moves on; windows over a Restore answer 409 code 19, an\n  update or merge_insert window 200; begin 0 deleted answers 200 empty before and after a restore;\n  the scratch table is stable and never refused; none of 299 listed tables is non-stable.\n- LH-194 (39a8b622): a live /produce on the existing head answers 202, keeps the location and\n  registers or deregisters nothing; the failing-seed half closes on its named offline proof\n  (owner ruling 2026-10-05): tests/integration/test_a_failed_seed_unwinds_only_the_registration_it_made.py.\n\nRegister: 199 open / 191 workable / 33 HIGH; short list 13 open with 25 enablers. Parked: LH-417\nto LH-420. Live pins: lance-rest-catalog and ingest lakehouse-dea984c5.\n\ntests: +0 −0\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"a497cfbffe9e616ba9fc6ba9ca89efab76f29732","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/a497cfbffe9e616ba9fc6ba9ca89efab76f29732"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/06faba82fc9b6cd6591e2992ba549f31c74d07d8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/06faba82fc9b6cd6591e2992ba549f31c74d07d8","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKDA2ZmFiYTgyZmM5YjZjZDY1OTFlMjk5MmJhNTQ5ZjMxYzc0ZDA3ZDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/dea984c5d7ddd33867b1428042c1b8d9b932a068","sha":"dea984c5d7ddd33867b1428042c1b8d9b932a068","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/dea984c5d7ddd33867b1428042c1b8d9b932a068"}],"sha":"06faba82fc9b6cd6591e2992ba549f31c74d07d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/06faba82fc9b6cd6591e2992ba549f31c74d07d8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/dea984c5d7ddd33867b1428042c1b8d9b932a068/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:31:47Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:54:16Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"fix(catalog): a write-tier vend reaches only data/, and /commit appends to a branch (LH-202)\n\nThe write tier granted Get/Put/Delete/AbortMultipartUpload on the whole\ntable prefix, so a can_write_data holder could commit Overwrite, Restore,\nUpdateBases or a DataReplacement straight against the store, move tags,\nforge branches, delete manifests and write the MemWAL. The branch write\nvend still carried Put/Delete on the branch''s own _versions/ and\n_transactions/.\n\nEach tier is now one FGA rung''s allow-list over the Lance layout\n(file_format.md):\n- read: list and get the prefix.\n- write (can_write_data): read, plus put/abort-upload on <prefix>/data/*\n  (tree/<b>/data/* on a branch) and put/delete on ingest''s\n  _ingest_staging/* ledger. Nothing under _versions/, _transactions/,\n  _deletions/, _indices/, _refs/, tree/ or _mem_wal/, and no delete.\n- maintain (can_maintain): get/put/delete on the whole prefix (on a branch,\n  the branch''s file directories), for compaction and cleanup. Also the\n  shape for the lineage outbox and the warehouse scope probe, which hold\n  no Lance layout.\n\nMeasured on pylance 12.0.0 (file_audit log plus a listing before and\nafter): write_fragments creates data/<file>.lance and data/<file>/<n>.blob\nonly; on a branch handle the same under tree/<b>/data/.\n\nThe credentials door checks the one rung a tier names: tier=write asks\ncan_write_data, tier=maintain asks can_maintain, never either-of, so a\nwriter cannot obtain the maintainer''s policy. Maintenance now vends\ntier=maintain; the outbox door and the scope probe vend maintain.\n\n/commit takes ?branch=: the append is judged and committed on the branch\n(files under tree/<b>/data/, branch-local read_version, commit through the\nbranch handle, lineage emitted on the branch). A missing branch is 404\nTableBranchNotFound. A run_id is recorded against main only, so a branch\ncommit carrying one is refused 400. No production writer committed\ndirectly with a vend: ingest already commits through /commit, maintenance\nholds the maintain tier, and the medallion lanes write with static keys\n(the commit-door decision, LH-330).\n\nResidue no session policy can refuse: a put over an existing data/ key\noverwrites a committed data file''s bytes.\n\nIngest''s staging directory name moves to service_kit.lakehouse.table_layout\nso the vend and the ledger read one constant. OpenAPI spec and TS client\nregenerated; chart, model.fga and skill prose follow the new tiers.\n\ntests: +2 -3\n- add tests/integration/test_a_write_vend_reaches_only_what_its_rung_may_change.py:\n  the session policy the real door sent to STS (moto), judged by moto''s IAM\n  evaluator per tier, with the prefix sibling refused at every tier; and\n  write_fragments + POST /commit landing rows on main and on a branch,\n  every object written being one the vended policy allows.\n- delete tests/unit/test_client_direct_commit.py::test_commit_appends_client_written_fragments,\n  tests/unit/test_vending.py::test_a_policy_does_not_reach_a_SIBLING_table_in_the_same_bucket\n  and ::test_a_read_tier_policy_cannot_write_its_own_table (covered by the\n  integration test).\n- rewrite the maintainer-rung tests (renamed ..._maintain_tier_vend.py)\n  for one rung per tier; the branch-directory test and the declared-base\n  test move to the maintain tier.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"79d1fc7805dc8a06dc05d8def8d8a630306ebd7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/79d1fc7805dc8a06dc05d8def8d8a630306ebd7c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/dea984c5d7ddd33867b1428042c1b8d9b932a068","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/dea984c5d7ddd33867b1428042c1b8d9b932a068","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKGRlYTk4NGM1ZDdkZGQzMzg2N2IxNDI4MDQyYzFiOGQ5YjkzMmEwNjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://gi