penapi-check reports drift on main. Generated output only.\n\ntests: +0 −0\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"8a6ff399d8fabeeaf424adb31765220ad3ac768a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/8a6ff399d8fabeeaf424adb31765220ad3ac768a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/fe0e40d57c02355631a600346770e9e2584e54c3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/fe0e40d57c02355631a600346770e9e2584e54c3","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKGZlMGU0MGQ1N2MwMjM1NTYzMWE2MDAzNDY3NzBlOWUyNTg0ZTU0YzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/3dfdd758beae5caefad4d4a84063a5e9b47fc534","sha":"3dfdd758beae5caefad4d4a84063a5e9b47fc534","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/3dfdd758beae5caefad4d4a84063a5e9b47fc534"}],"sha":"fe0e40d57c02355631a600346770e9e2584e54c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/fe0e40d57c02355631a600346770e9e2584e54c3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/3dfdd758beae5caefad4d4a84063a5e9b47fc534/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:27:11Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:47:56Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"fix(catalog): a change window is one snapshot at its end and refuses what the version columns cannot describe (LH-241)\n\nLance''s change data feed is three queries against one snapshot\n(lance_docs/file_format.md:4270-4298). /changes answered a closed window\nfrom the latest snapshot, read none of the window''s transactions, and the\npublished contract told consumers to key on `_row_created_at_version`.\n\n- dataplane.read_changes answers all three kinds from the dataset opened\n  AT end_version (the head it read, for an open window), so a closed window\n  answers the same set however far the table moved on. The door makes one\n  call for every kind.\n- The window''s transactions are read and a window spanning a Restore, an\n  Overwrite, or an Update with non-empty fields_modified is refused (409,\n  InvalidTableState, \"resynchronise from begin_version=0\"). Measured on\n  pylance 12.0.0: update_columns commits Update(fields_modified=[f]) and\n  leaves _row_last_updated_at_version unmoved; dataset.update and\n  merge_insert commit Update(fields_modified=[]); compaction is a\n  ReserveFragments BaseOperation then a Rewrite. A window from version 0 is\n  the whole snapshot and skips the walk.\n- A branch window is split at the branch point: versions at or below\n  parent_version are read on the parent''s handle\n  (checkout_version((parent_branch, v))), so the walk never reads the\n  branch''s first manifest, whose read_transaction panics on 12.0.0, and the\n  deleted feed runs one delta() per span (delta() on a branch refuses a\n  begin below its branch point). Any unreadable transaction refuses the\n  window; the read catches BaseException for the pyo3 panic, as the\n  existing committed-version walk does.\n- After maintenance cleanup: the window''s begin manifest must exist (delta()\n  reads it), so a window whose begin was cleaned is refused 409 for every\n  kind alike, and a `deleted` window from version 0 answers empty without\n  calling delta(), whose version-1 manifest cleanup removes. The prescribed\n  resync from begin_version=0 therefore works on a cleaned table.\n- The consumer rule is stated once, in catalog.services.changes: resolve\n  (from, to] through /changes inserted/updated/deleted, or merge by key on\n  _row_last_updated_at_version plus the deleted stream. The six published\n  range statements point at it, and runners/dummy follows it (it read\n  _row_created_at_version only, so an in-place correction and a deletion\n  never reached silver).\n\ntests: +3 -0 (collected cases +12)\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"46f04cbeb51194a8e9da70ad409efbf97f986188","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/46f04cbeb51194a8e9da70ad409efbf97f986188"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/3dfdd758beae5caefad4d4a84063a5e9b47fc534","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/3dfdd758beae5caefad4d4a84063a5e9b47fc534","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKDNkZmRkNzU4YmVhZTVjYWVmYWQ0ZDRhODQwNjNhNWU5YjQ3ZmM1MzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/9f66a9eace1a1b1945a6a29b9711cf6e98734faa","sha":"9f66a9eace1a1b1945a6a29b9711cf6e98734faa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/9f66a9eace1a1b1945a6a29b9711cf6e98734faa"}],"sha":"3dfdd758beae5caefad4d4a84063a5e9b47fc534","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/3dfdd758beae5caefad4d4a84063a5e9b47fc534"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/9f66a9eace1a1b1945a6a29b9711cf6e98734faa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:20:11Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:47:56Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"fix(catalog): the change feed and the cascade refuse a table without stable row ids, and a retraction reads Lance''s deletion record (LH-216)\n\nWithout stable row ids `_rowid` is a physical address that compaction\nrewrites and Lance tracks no row versions (lance_docs/file_format.md:\n4011-4015). Measured on pylance 12.0.0: such a table still answers both\nversion columns, both read 1 for every row, and an `inserted` window over\na real append answers [] with a 200.\n\n- /changes refuses such a table (409, InvalidTableState) for every kind,\n  before any predicate runs; the false changes.py precondition paragraph is\n  rewritten to the measured behaviour.\n- The register door refuses a dataset without stable row ids (400), at a\n  fresh registration and on the 409 converge arm, as it does flag 256.\n- stage_stamp.carry_source_rowid / stamp_stage take the upstream''s\n  `stable_row_ids` and refuse to mint `source_rowid` from an upstream\n  without them (UnstableRowIdsError). Every in-process mint site in\n  medallion compute.py and every Ray-lane stamp in scripts/ray_stage_job.py\n  goes through it.\n- The Ray delta lane retracts from Lance''s own record:\n  `upstream.delta(begin_version=base).get_deleted_row_ids()`, mapped through\n  the upstream at the boundary at deeper hops, with a 1:N survivor check\n  that filters on the candidate keys. No key column is read whole on either\n  side, and a compaction (no deleted row) retracts nothing. A non-stable\n  upstream is refused. UpstreamVanishedError goes: an empty upstream scan can\n  no longer be misread as \"delete the tier\".\n- Test fixtures that wrote non-stable upstreams now create them with stable\n  row ids.\n\nNot done: the How''s \"align seed_bronze''s id field with the ingest\nprimary-key metadata\". Declaring `lance-schema:unenforced-primary-key` on\nseed_bronze''s `id` made\nservices/medallion/tests/test_a_stage_rerun_carries_what_its_upstream_holds_now.py\nfail on the second transform_stage merge with \"Primary key column and all\nits ancestors must not be nullable\"; reverted, cause not diagnosed.\n\ntests: +3 -1 (collected cases +7 -1)\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"dc3006484e470ae170b99408f44575d2e223c994","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/dc3006484e470ae170b99408f44575d2e223c994"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/9f66a9eace1a1b1945a6a29b9711cf6e98734faa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.g