.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/725c33eb4e20450c7dea6c64d920cd419d4454b6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:22:37Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:22:37Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"chore(estate): LH-213 and LH-217 close at helm rev 280; LH-245 fails live; CP-056 opens the full engine split\n\nRev 280 (lance-rest-catalog lakehouse-4a5027c7 on every lakehouse deployment), health at\n17:17:03Z, 15 min after the rollout settled: DLQ unchanged (ingest 1, lineage 1, both from\nbefore), no pod unready or restarted.\n\n- LH-213 (91754e62) closes on named offline proof (owner ruling 2026-10-05):\n  test_a_stage_rerun_carries_what_its_upstream_holds_now.py.\n- LH-217 (4a5027c7) closes on named offline proof (same ruling): its two tests in the\n  carried-blob seam (3 cases).\n- LH-245 (c620de1f) stays open. Live probe on a scratch table: K1 pass; K2 fail (keys present\n  after 964 s, 8 ticks, zero disarm lines); K3 fail (three insert-door appends deleted versions\n  1 and 2). The sweep never visited the table: the queue lane finishes about 5 visits a minute\n  against 606 work orders per 120 s tick (LH-195), and the design leaves writers armed until\n  the sweep arrives. The row records the finding and the next fix (the committing door strips\n  the keys before it commits).\n- CP-056 added with the owner''s approval (2026-10-05, full BYO split): the lakehouse ships the\n  Ray adapter, both Ray job scripts and an engine registry that hard-codes Ray. CP-044 moves out\n  of AFTER LAUNCH as its enabler.\n\nRegister: 203 open / 195 workable / 35 HIGH; short list 17 open with 25 enablers. Live pins:\n