rask/commits/c620de1f3661568f16b4616b2435c6754afd7ab3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T16:17:17Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T16:43:16Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"fix(maintenance): the sweep is the one reclaimer, and no writer''s commit deletes a version (LH-245)\n\nLance''s commit-path auto-cleanup deletes inside whichever writer commits, every N commits, from the\nlance.auto_cleanup.* manifest keys (lance_docs/guide.md:3857-3923). Measured on pylance 12.0.0: with\ninterval=1 and older_than=0s, one ordinary append took versions 1..7 to 7..8, and a commit of an\nAppend (the catalog /commit shape) did the same, past a legal hold and a protected base, under the\nwriter''s identity and recorded nowhere. pylance 12''s write_dataset has no skip_auto_cleanup.\n\nThe lane is retired rather than governed: nothing can establish that maintenance is a table''s sole\nwriter. auto_cleanup_interval_commits leaves PolicyRequest, PolicyResponse, DatasetPlan, compact_one,\nthe OpenAPI spec and both zones'' policy schemas. compact_one deletes every lance.auto_cleanup.* key\nright after the open, before the nested-branch, manifest-flag and protected-base refusals, and only\nwhen a key is present (delete_config_keys commits a version even with nothing to delete). All keys\nunder the prefix, because disable_auto_cleanup leaves retain_versions standing. The write probe counts\nan armed table as may-write so a vended credential signs the disarm. DatasetResult and the sweep\nsummary report auto_cleanup_disarmed in place of auto_cleanup_configured.\n\nretain_versions needs no mapping onto Lance''s key: with the lane closed it reaches\ncleanup_old_versions, which honours it. The regenerated OpenAPI spec and client also carry the\nerasure and vend descriptions LH-263 and LH-203 changed without regenerating.\n\nNot covered: a table its policy skips this tick is not opened, so its keys wait for a tick that\nmaintains it. tests/unit/test_maintenance_optimize.py still holds three tests of the retired lane\n(test_handing_cleanup_to_the_dataset_skips_our_own_sweep, test_a_LEGAL_HOLD_beats_auto_cleanup,\ntest_auto_cleanup_does_not_COMMIT_A_VERSION_when_already_configured); they fail until the prune pass\nthat owns the file deletes them.\n\ntests: +2 -3 (test_no_commit_but_the_sweeps_reclaims_a_version.py: one test per closes-when clause,\nthe first parametrized over hold and protected base; three lane tests to delete in a file this commit\nmay not edit, net -1 once they go; test_maintenance_policies.py''s round-trip moved off the retired\nfield onto cleanup_enabled)\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"2a5e28571bb899332847e189ab0ec60795465ada","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/2a5e28571bb899332847e189ab0ec60795465ada"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/c620de1f3661568f16b4616b2435c6754afd7ab3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/c620de1f3661568f16b4616b2435c6754afd7ab3","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKGM2MjBkZTFmMzY2MTU2OGYxNmI0NjE2YjI0MzVjNjc1NGFmZDdhYjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/91754e62494b75609e23d9f1a0a8a7035c3350fc","sha":"91754e62494b75609e23d9f1a0a8a7035c3350fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/91754e62494b75609e23d9f1a0a8a7035c3350fc"}],"sha":"c620de1f3661568f16b4616b2435c6754afd7ab3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/c620de1f3661568f16b4616b2435c6754afd7ab3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/91754e62494b75609e23d9f1a0a8a7035c3350fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T16:15:52Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T16:43:16Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"fix(medallion): a stage re-run writes what its upstream holds now, and adds a column by id (LH-213)\n\nThe in-process stage skipped its write when the target''s columns were a subset of the run''s output\nand the source_rowid lists matched. Values were never compared: a bronze row corrected in place keeps\nits stable _rowid and position, so the correction never reached silver and silver kept the first\nrun''s lineage. Its add-columns branch aligned by position through a handle opened after the check,\nand when the lists differed the full-sync fallback could not widen (merge_insert refuses a source\ncolumn the target lacks, pylance 12.0.0), so that stage failed on every retry.\n\nThe skip is deleted: every run ends in the full-sync merge_insert on id, carrying corrected values\nand this run''s lineage. A new column is added first with LanceDataset.merge(out.select([\"id\", *new]),\nleft_on=\"id\") on the handle that read the schema; Lance refuses that Merge when another commit passed\nits read version, and the tier is re-read (at most three attempts).\n\nCost: a redelivery the in-process idempotency key does not catch now rewrites the tier; LH-212''s\nconditioned merge restores that no-op by comparing values.\n\nDocs: DECISIONS entry; medallion-data-flow.md section 6 table rewritten (it described the skip).\n\ntests: +2 -3 (test_a_stage_rerun_carries_what_its_upstream_holds_now.py replaces\ntest_additive_stage_adds_columns.py''s two tests; tests/unit/test_medallion_compute.py drops the\ntest that pinned the redelivery no-op)\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"fee725037d34d51fbe89589e8690889ac297c2ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/fee725037d34d51fbe89589e8690889ac297c2ca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/91754e62494b75609e23d9f1a0a8a7035c3350fc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"