","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/e7c9413acc7ddfa8195d484363c28ea1f17bb2d1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T14:08:07Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T14:32:39Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"fix(catalog): one dataset location has one holder, and nothing destroys bytes another id resolves to (LH-204)\n\nThe dir backend arbitrates only object-id ADDs: a register at an occupied\nlocation commits and concurrent deregisters of one id all succeed. Measured\non pylance 12.0.0, eight barrier-threaded renames of one source left eight\nlive ids on one dataset in 4 of 4 rounds, so retiring the source first\narbitrated nothing.\n\n- service_kit.lakehouse.location_claims: one claim per location on the\n  control root (_locations/<sha256 of the decoded path>.json), created\n  put-if-not-exists and handed over under its ETag; a holder that no longer\n  resolves to its location is taken over only after a 15-minute lease.\n- rename hands the claim from source to destination before either backend\n  call, stamped with a per-request token so renames into ONE destination\n  are not each other''s retry; losers answer 409 ConcurrentModification\n  (code 14); a failed retire or destination register hands it back, except\n  when the destination already resolves to the location (the winner stands).\n- register and both undrops take the claim (held: 400 InvalidInput /\n  409 InvalidTableState); recoverable drops keep it for the trashed id;\n  destructive drop, destructive cascade, deregister and the purge release it.\n- a destructive drop, and a destructive cascade before destroying anything,\n  refuses 409 InvalidTableState while the claim names another live holder.\n- register refuses a location over the model registry or artifact tree.\n- maintenance purge reads table locations from __manifest as well as ids\n  and refuses a record whose location a live table resolves into.\n- records.create_json on a local root links a staged file into place and\n  read_json takes a shared lock, so a reader never sees a half-written\n  record (an empty claim read under eight concurrent renames).\n\ntests: +3 -2 (concurrent renames through the catalog app, to distinct and\nto one destination; the purge sparing aliased bytes; a destructive drop\nand cascade of an alias refused; the sequential-rename and call-order\nrename tests they replace are deleted; the register refusal loop and the\nfailed-retire test are extended)\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"cf1a032d17af665d4823cf772c41ac1a2a49a626","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/cf1a032d17af665d4823cf772c41ac1a2a49a626"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/e7c9413acc7ddfa8195d484363c28ea1f17bb2d1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/e7c9413acc7ddfa8195d484363c28ea1f17bb2d1","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKGU3Yzk0MTNhY2M3ZGRmYTgxOTVkNDg0MzYzYzI4ZWExZjE3YmIyZDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/3abc66953e536ebb7816295f6358b7fa74e36fdd","sha":"3abc66953e536ebb7816295f6358b7fa74e36fdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/3abc66953e536ebb7816295f6358b7fa74e36fdd"}],"sha":"e7c9413acc7ddfa8195d484363c28ea1f17bb2d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/e7c9413acc7ddfa8195d484363c28ea1f17bb2d1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/3abc66953e536ebb7816295f6358b7fa74e36fdd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T14:09:44Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T14:23:05Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"fix(catalog,maintenance): a write event names the commit the write made, its ref and the branch''s incarnation (LH-214)\n\nEvery catalog write door now states the version its own commit made, and\nemit_measured_write takes pin_version and branch with no default:\n\n- main insert goes through the handle path branches use (the dir\n  backend''s insert_into_table answers {} on pylance 12.0.0), so the\n  response and the event carry the handle''s own commit, and\n  num_inserted_rows is the payload''s row count;\n- /commit pins the version it committed; update, delete, schema\n  metadata, the in-pod compact and reindex pass their branch;\n- restore, native schema metadata and the index doors resolve their\n  transaction_id with DescribeTransaction (dataplane.committed_version);\n  on a branch, where the dir describe_transaction reads main only, by a\n  bounded walk of the branch''s handle that stops above the branch point\n  and survives a pylance panic;\n- a commit that cannot be identified emits versionless, not latest;\n- a branch write carries lance.branchIdentifier (the last uuid of\n  pylance''s branch_identifier chain); list_branches metadata, the branch\n  created/deleted and tag control events carry it too, and tag events\n  name the ref the tag pins;\n- the queued index worker emits the version and ref it built on, off the\n  building handle rather than a reopen of main.\n\ntests: +4 -4 (new test_a_write_event_names_the_commit_it_made: concurrent\nappends, every branch door, a recreated branch, a branch lookup past the\nbranch point; the index-worker test is\nextended to the emit; removed the mock insert-version test, the two\nfacet/trailer ref tests in test_a_branch_write_names_its_ref and the\nadd_columns lineage test in test_column_branch, which the new file covers)\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"49868ad81e7ef814ce6fd57ea6bb3b8ae936d707","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/49868ad81e7ef814ce6fd57ea6bb3b8ae936d707"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/3abc66953e536ebb7816295f6358b7fa74e36fdd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/3abc66953e536ebb7816295f6358b7fa74e36fdd","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKDNhYmM2Njk1M2U1MzZlYmI3ODE2Mjk1ZjYzNThiN2ZhNzRlMzZmZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/7360d1dae6a56a28bf95c71462a62621d8a6b6fa","sha":"7360d1dae6a56a28bf95c71462a62621d8a6b6fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/7360d1dae6a56a28bf95c71462a62621d8a6b6fa"}],"sha":"3abc66953e536ebb7816295f6358b7fa74e36fdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/3abc66953e536ebb7816295f6358b7fa74e36fdd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/7360d1dae6a56a28bf95c71462a62621d8a6b6fa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T14:04:10Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T14:13:34Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"fix(catalog,maintenance): a branch''s directory holds only its own files (LH-203)\n\nThe format joins a branch name verbatim onto tree/, so `a/b` lives inside tree/a/ and `a/_versions`\ninside branch a''s version directory, and Lance reads whatever lies there as a''s. Measured on pylance\n12.0.0: a reclaim of `a` deleted `a/_versions`''s manifests (cold read: Not found), deleting\n`a/_versions` deleted a''s history, and deleting `a` under `a/b` removed only the ref.\n\n- service_kit.lakehouse.branch_layout holds the rule: the five directories a branch writes, the\n  reserved segment names, nesting, and reading a name back from _refs/branches.\n- create refuses a layout segment (400, 13) and a name that nests with an existing branch (409, 19).\n- a branch-write vend grants tree/<b>/{_versions,_transactions,_deletions,_indices,data}/*.\n- delete goes through nested branches deepest first; a branch inside another''s file directories is\n  refused 409; a missing name, or a branch outside the set forked from a member of it, is refused\n  (404 / 409, code 19) before anything is deleted.\n- the credentials door''s OpenAPI text names the branch''s own directories, not tree/<branch>/*.\n- the sweep (refused_by=nested_branch), maintenance/run and version/delete refuse to reclaim a branch\n  with another inside it.\n- discover_datasets lists branches from _refs/branches instead of walking tree/.\n\nNot done: describe still refuses a non-main branch with vend_credentials; erasure''s per-ref reclaim\ndoes not ask the nested-branch gate; a write vend for `a` still reaches a legacy `a/_versions`.\n\ntests: +5 -3 (vend policy test replaced by an IAM-evaluated one; discovery FakeFS test replaced by a\nreal-pylance one; three integration tests through the catalog app; the MagicMock delete-routing test\npruned, now driven for real).\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"e96628404bfa64b0d72c297686a1aef7954e083a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/e96628404bfa64b0d72c297686a1aef7954e083a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/7360d1dae6a56a28bf95c71462a62621d8a6b6fa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/u