ntry (default s3://<bucket>/models/) and the\nvend allowlist unioned that list, so every plain create''s read vend granted <bucket>/models/*, a\ncreate pointing Blob.from_uri at another tenant''s weights was accepted, /commit accepted a\ndescriptor through any manifest base equal to a configured entry, and the read judge sanctioned\nany plain base inside a configured entry, so a planted models/<victim>/ base was served by the\nblob door and recorded by register.\n\n- create: registers one external base only when the request names it in the door''s hidden\n  external_blob_base query parameter (rask_params.RaskExternalBlobBase, beside data_base; never a\n  schema or property key, which LH-208 refuses), on a blob-v2 table, inside an approved entry, and\n  covering no governed storage (base_judge.GovernedStorage: catalog, control, model registry and\n  artifact roots, reserved and warehouse-claimed buckets); ingest''s catalog client sends its\n  approved base there, and a stage runner''s ensure_stage_output its upstream''s manifest base\n- /commit: a kind-3 descriptor resolves only through a base the table''s record holds as external_blob\n- read and register: a configured base that covers governed storage is sanctioned by the record\n  alone (BaseJudge.judge, entries_for_registration); maintenance and lineage protection unchanged\n- vend: pointer bases (CONFIGURED or recorded external_blob) are dropped from the grant, still direct;\n  vend_sanctioned_bases deleted, the vendor allowlist is LANCE_MULTIBASE_DATA_BASES alone\n\ntests: +7 -2 (new test_an_external_blob_base_is_authorized_per_table.py: 2 vend, 2 create, a stage\noutput taking carried pointers, and a model-tree base refused at the blob door and register; a\nplanted-base case in the LH-211 forged-fragment test, whose ingest commit test now creates its table\nthrough ingest''s own catalog client; the two settings tests pinning the reversed allowlist union\ndeleted)\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/sessi