_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/ac30f3b1520a4a8d3b210a0a1b1a3f3edb40aafa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T10:37:22Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T10:51:33Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"feat(medallion): a Ray run is a plan closed by its job''s outcome door or a sweep, and stage_run and train_run are deleted (CP-029)\n\nCriterion 3: the cascade learned a stage''s or a training run''s outcome only through the Dapr workflows\nstage_run and train_run polling Ray. Now (docs/DECISIONS.md, the CP-029 entry):\n- Each Ray run has a plan record in the control root, keyed by derive_idempotency_key with code_version\n  (clause a), created if absent and closed by CAS (first terminal wins), and announced as run_planned on\n  catalog.control.v1 (the BYO-engine seam).\n- The job reports its own outcome to an idempotent door on the app that planned it (stage runner or\n  producer), authenticated by the Ray head''s projected rask-medallion token, admitted on that route only.\n- One resolution function serves the door and a bindings.cron sweep, so a run reaches exactly one\n  terminal: SUCCEEDED hands off to pass 2 and is never FAILed (clause b); a lost job with the commit\n  marker (rask.action_id / rask.run_id in the transaction_properties of its last commit) is stage-ready\n  or COMPLETE with that version (clauses c, d); FAILED after a commit names the committed version\n  (clause e); RUNNING at any age emits nothing.\n- Marked merges keep Lance''s conflict retry (re-run execute_uncommitted on a retryable conflict).\n- Terminate, on both lanes, re-reads Ray after the stop and resolves through the same function.\n- A marker read through a store outage raises instead of reading as \"no marker\".\n\nReview: one adversarial round per lane. Stage lane: HIGH (marked merges had lost the conflict retry), fixed;\nthree LOWs that broke the spec or the history rule, fixed; four LOWs parked. Train lane: MEDIUM (terminate\nFAILed a job whose model was committed), fixed; the history docstring, fixed; two LOWs parked.\n\ntests: +7 -66 (clause tests a, b, d, e, c and the resubmit budget replace test_stage_workflow.py,\ntest_train_workflow.py, test_cascade_operator_surface.py and the workflow cases of their seams);\nfleet lane 6018 -> 5954 collected, all green.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"3e58cde1b7494b5e5138a24a3d113f4a0f9bbafa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/3e58cde1b7494b5e5138a24a3d113f4a0f9bbafa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/ac30f3b1520a4a8d3b210a0a1b1a3f3edb40aafa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.gith