url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/4ff49c1ae96ffa0f2a638970e1e5d8a279e31216/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T16:57:21Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T16:57:21Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"test(xc078): the signature-door tests swap in their counters and never reload a metrics module\n\nTRIAGE row S (and W). The notifications door test''s signature_counts fixture\nreloaded notifications.api.metrics, which made new Lane, Outcome, PassOutcome\nand Door classes. reconcile_cron keeps the PassOutcome it imported and\nrecord_pass compares members by identity, so after the reload every pass count\nwas 0: in CI''s serial run (collection order, this file before\ntest_reconcile_cron.py) two reconcile tests failed every time, and about one run\nin three under -n 16.\n\nEach signature-door fixture (notifications, maintenance, lineage) now runs its\nmetrics module''s code into a module object of its own under the meter of a\nMeterProvider carrying an InMemoryMetricReader, and monkeypatches only the\nsignature counters onto the imported module. The counters'' names stay the\nmodule''s own, so the tests pin the series the alerts read (renaming any of the\nthree refusal instruments turns all 24 door cases red; the maintenance test\npreviously stood the counters in with a _Counter fake and pinned no name), and\nno other module attribute is replaced.\n\nSerial run, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 uv run pytest services/notifications/tests -p no:cacheprovider -q`:\n  before: 2 failed, 341 passed (test_an_overlapping_tick_is_skipped_rather_than_run_twice,\n          test_a_completed_tick_is_counted_and_BOTH_pass_outcomes_have_a_series)\n  after:  343 passed\n\ntests: +0 -0 (collected cases unchanged)\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"524b61c2f3396b5e35a8b2e7c6b0f13ed908eeff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/524b61c2f3396b5e35a8b2e7c6b0f13ed908eeff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/4ff49c1ae96ffa0f2a638970e1e5d8a279e31216","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/4ff49c1ae96ffa0f2a638970e1e5d8a279e31216","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKDRmZjQ5YzFhZTk2ZmZhMGYyYTYzODk3MGUxZTVkOGEyNzllMzEyMTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/73ed05f5833e7029ce9a8c532c6a53a50c137dc9","sha":"73ed05f5833e7029ce9a8c532c6a53a50c137dc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/73ed05f5833e7029ce9a8c532c6a53a50c137dc9"}],"sha":"4ff49c1ae96ffa0f2a638970e1e5d8a279e31216","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/4ff49c1ae96ffa0f2a638970e1e5d8a279e31216"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/b0215a7e9f5477161c1ab9930b6a7ba5786ee67e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T16:54:40Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T16:54:40Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"fix(xc078): the bronze head lists the declared lanes at most once per delivery, off the event loop\n\nTriage row E (XC-078 slice 1 review). `_bronze_write` asked `_has_declared_lane` per output, and\neach call was a `transform_specs.list_specs`: one LIST plus one GET per stored declaration, on the\nevent loop, before the signature door. An event naming N outputs cost N listings, so ~28k outputs\nheld the loop past /livez, and the door could not protect it.\n\n`_declared_inputs(settings, project=...)` returns the declared input tables from one listing, and\n`_bronze_write` reaches it through a per-call `functools.cache`: listed only once an output is not\nthe configured pair, and at most once per delivery. /bronze-arrival decides in a worker thread\n(`run_in_threadpool(bronze_arrival_of, ...)`), so a listing never holds the loop. Still only what\nwould act is verified: the selection runs before the door, as before.\n\ntests: +0 -0 (functions).\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"a0f63bfb31598086e3a7becfe2c6e9595f3c868d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/a0f63bfb31598086e3a7becfe2c6e9595f3c868d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/b0215a7e9f5477161c1ab9930b6a7ba5786ee67e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/b0215a7e9f5477161c1ab993