s","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T16:53:12Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T16:53:12Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"test(xc078): RED - the bronze head lists the declared lanes once per output, on the event loop\n\nTriage row E (XC-078 slice 1 review). Deciding whether /bronze-arrival acts on a write it does not\nrecognise reads the declared lanes, and `_has_declared_lane` called `transform_specs.list_specs`\n(one LIST and one GET per stored declaration) once per output, synchronously, before the door. The\nreviewer''s repro: 2000 outputs, 2000 listings, 4.1 s with a 2 ms stub, the loop held throughout.\n\nThe door test now runs with the control root the chart renders on the producer and a registry\ndouble carrying `list_specs`'' signature, which records each listing and whether it ran on the event\nloop. A case `listed` count is asserted on every delivery: the silver write lists once, a new case\nnaming three silver tables must list once, every listing in a worker thread.\n\nFails on its own assertion: three listings on the event loop for three outputs, and the single\nlisting of the silver case on the event loop.\n\ntests: +0 -0 (functions); collected cases +1 (door test parametrized cases 20 -> 21).\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"a134727f159457d9b9bf9296cf523a9cae3c3db5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/a134727f159457d9b9bf9296cf523a9cae3c3db5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/95bee7fddd648b8fb7a3bfccf27bd4f3571fe8b7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/95bee7fddd648b8fb7a3bfccf27bd4f3571fe8b7","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKDk1YmVlN2ZkZGQ2NDhiOGZiN2EzYmZjY2YyN2JkNGYzNTcxZmU4Yjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/69a546329ee67913d93694727d8587925ca3a5e9","sha":"69a546329ee67913d93694727d8587925ca3a5e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/69a546329ee67913d93694727d8587925ca3a5e9"}],"sha":"95bee7fddd648b8fb7a3bfccf27bd4f3571fe8b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/95bee7fddd648b8fb7a3bfccf27bd4f3571fe8b7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/73ed05f5833e7029ce9a8c532c6a53a50c137dc9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T16:52:01Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T16:52:01Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"fix(xc078): every signature-refusal series exists at 0 from its door''s registration, so the first refusal pages\n\nTRIAGE row D, the notifications, maintenance and lineage half (the medallion is\nanother change). Each service''s metrics module gains\ncreate_signature_refused_series(), which adds 0 to every series of its refusal\ncounter over the closed label sets: notifications Door x RefusalReason (24),\nmaintenance SignatureDoor x RefusalReason (12), lineage RefusalReason (12, the\nLH-064 rule has the same defect). The door registration calls it:\nregister_subscriptions, register_arrival_route (only when the door is\nregistered) and register_dapr. In production each runs after the\nMeterProvider is installed, by make_service_app for notifications and by\nopentelemetry-instrument at interpreter start for maintenance and lineage; an\nadd through the proxy meter before that is dropped (measured on\nopentelemetry-sdk 1.44.0).\n\nchart/alerting/rules_test.yml group 1f modelled a steady climb (0+1x14), which\nhid the defect. Each series is now the 0 its service creates followed by ONE\nrefusal held flat (0x4 1x10), evaluated at 8m. Measured with promtool 2.55.1: a\nsingle refusal at 5m fires from 7m and resolves at 10m, when its 0 sample leaves\nthe 5m window, so the former 10m eval time cannot see it.\n\n  promtool check rules rules.yml      -> SUCCESS: 59 rules found\n  promtool test rules rules_test.yml  -> SUCCESS\n\ntests: +0 -0 (promtool cases unchanged in number; group 1f series and eval times changed)\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"ace183b1ac371bdb34942a7caac909940e33de97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/ace183b1ac371bdb34942a7caac909940e33de97"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/73ed05f5833e7029ce9a8c532c6a53a50c137dc9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/73ed05f5833e7029ce9a8c532c6a53a50c137dc9","node_id":"C_kwDOSh8U4doAKDczZWQwNWY1ODMzZTcwMjljZTlhOGM1MzJjNmE1M2E1MGMxMzdkYzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commit/2388378c550c859a60b41591503311db23e1f13c","sha":"2388378c550c859a60b41591503311db23e1f13c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/2388378c550c859a60b41591503311db23e1f13c"}],"sha":"73ed05f5833e7029ce9a8c532c6a53a50c137dc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/73ed05f5833e7029ce9a8c532c6a53a50c137dc9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Borg93","id":48671678,"login":"Borg93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjcxNjc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/commits/69a546329ee67913d93694727d8587925ca3a5e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T16:51:32Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T16:51:32Z","email":"Borg93@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Borg93"},"message":"fix(xc078): the bronze head ignores maintenance passes, and admits only the producer and the catalog\n\nOwner ruling R7 (XC-078 slice 1).\n\nThe head (`ingest_trigger._bronze_write`) acted on any COMPLETE naming the bronze pair except a\nbyte-free catalog marker. A maintenance pass is such an event: the catalog resolves the tenant on\nevery write it announces, so its compact_table or create_index on a project''s bronze table names\nexactly the qualified pair, under a signature that verifies, and started a cascade no batch brought.\n`_MAINTENANCE_OPERATIONS` = {compaction, compact_table, create_index}, the emitters'' own spelling\n(maintenance''s COMPACTION and CREATE_INDEX, the catalog''s COMPACT_TABLE and CREATE_INDEX; the set\nlineage keys its maintenance rung on), copied rather than imported as maintenance copies its loop\nguard. Ignored before the signature door: acknowledged, never verified, no trigger.\n\nWith maintenance passes ignored, the producer''s RASK_EVENT_SIGNERS narrows to the identities of the\nroles medallion_producer and catalog: `lance.doorEnv` takes an optional third argument, the signer\nroles, and the producer passes those two. Only the producer''s own /produce and /ingest-media events\nand the catalog''s write announcements fire the head; ingest never publishes to the lineage topic.\nThe producer reads RASK_EVENT_SIGNERS for /bronze-arrival alone. RASK_EVENT_DELEGATORS stays the\ncatalog everywhere. Notifications and both maintenance Deployments keep lineage''s full sets. The why\nlives in values.yaml `signing.doors`, not in a template comment.\n\nRendered with signing.doors=enforce: the producer carries [\"service-catalog\",\n\"service-medallion-producer\"]; notifications, maintenance and maintenance-worker carry lineage''s seven.\n\ntests: +0 -0 (functions).\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017XnXD48toDdU7HLsHN54Sv","tree":{"sha":"eb2b147a767e8aa89a204dbd5d1cf9542410ba6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/trees/eb2b147a767e8aa89a204dbd5d1cf9542410ba6c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Riksarkivet/rask/git/commits/69a546329ee67913d93694727d8587925ca3a5e9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48671678?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Borg93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"ht