/api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Arc-E-Tect/sedr-wiremock-spring-restdocs/commits/46f7d8ea1a94f8812e3486e961c00fcb18cd1df6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T20:37:20Z","email":"iwan@arc-e-tect.com","name":"Iwan Eising"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T20:37:20Z","email":"iwan@arc-e-tect.com","name":"Iwan Eising"},"message":"fix(pre-commit): skip Spring REST Docs description files and ignore IntelliJ bin/ output\n\n- .githooks/pre-commit: added skip rule for files matching `-descriptions.properties`\n  Spring REST Docs description files use property keys like\n  `request_field.password` and `request_header.x_api_key` to name\n  the API field being described; the value is human-readable documentation\n  text, not a credential. The secret-scanning regex matched these key\n  names and produced false positives that blocked legitimate source commits.\n  The skip rule targets the naming convention explicitly (`*-descriptions.properties`)\n  rather than widening or weakening the secret pattern itself.\n\n- red-thread/.gitignore: added `bin` entry alongside the existing `build` entry\n  IntelliJ IDEA compiles project resources to `bin/` (parallel to Gradle''s\n  `build/`) when its own build system is active. The five Spring Boot service\n  subprojects each had a `bin/` directory with resource copies staged for\n  commit. These are IDE-generated artefacts and must not be version-controlled.\n  The entry covers all subproject `bin/` directories because `.gitignore`\n  rules apply recursively from the file''s location.","tree":{"sha":"e3fb894a791676f2df0fa5e56eae8d6b3689a08b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Arc-E-Tect/sedr-wiremock-spring-restdocs/git/trees/e3fb894a791676f2df0fa5e56eae8d6b3689a08b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Arc-E-Tect/sedr-wiremock-spring-restdocs/git/commits/46f7d8ea1a94f8812e3486e961c00fcb18cd1df6","verification":{"payload":"tree e3fb894a791676f2df0fa5e56eae8d6b3689a08b\nparent 8cc4b4cd344db632b0c80ca3181226d11ad0f7de\nauthor Iwan Eising <iwan@arc-e-tect.com> 1779223040 +0400\ncommitter Iwan Eising <iwan@arc-e-tect.com> 1779223040 +0400\n\nfix(pre-commit): skip Spring REST Docs description files and ignore IntelliJ bin/ output\n\n- .githooks/pre-commit: added skip rule for files matching `-descriptions.properties`\n  Spring REST Docs description files use property keys like\n  `request_field.password` and `request_header.x_api_key` to name\n  the API field being described; the value is human-readable documentation\n  text, not a credential. The secret-scanning regex matched these key\n  names and produced false positives that blocked legitimate source commits.\n  The skip rule targets the naming convention explicitly (`*-descriptions.properties`)\n  rather than widening or weakening the secret pattern itself.\n\n- red-thread/.gitignore: added `bin` entry alongside the existing `build` entry\n  IntelliJ IDEA compiles project resources to `bin/` (parallel to Gradle''s\n  `build/`) when its own build system is active. The five Spring Boot service\n  subprojects each had a `bin/` directory with resource copies staged for\n  commit. These are IDE-generated artefacts and must not be version-controlled.\n  The entry covers all subproject `bin/` directories because `.gitignore`\n  rules apply recursively from the file''s location.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCAAdFiEEp0rumQkFq+V/pwSu4yo0Jx0mac0FAmoMygAACgkQ4yo0Jx0m\nac3oxg//btifsqo2I29ew9jc+zRt+OewH6Z3zutmp7BJZKVotilSy/zh/gtLgajo\nLjhy1Jr4xgbB2fly8jaRh+zQ1IJM3v+b++XS5JDb831gvp5AkD36BarBc3AWTPlR\n39+RnfSzXkv5WzvMJtJyGvln5CLSWlBNXR03Y2VHrm6RgDZMbxnZyhT5gR0QIpGA\n4yNE99k6m34GiKt0WNgjjwPwyQ3eq132mIyfx/uxak97fdERschNyzt5sUjZTBmZ\nW5NH+mtVtypgQm1rbC9lkLb7pFQrD/KRj2d9x+wwB6g4MFgwNShTFHLBsKNmVfYl\nda0/WzXMJhZh0lCt0N7YQ5AHLw/Sw29VkwiqaNtXxezyZ2fhmlw