ect/sedr-wiremock-spring-restdocs/commits/46f7d8ea1a94f8812e3486e961c00fcb18cd1df6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12331140?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Arc-E-Tect","id":12331140,"login":"Arc-E-Tect","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzMxMTQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Arc-E-Tect/sedr-wiremock-spring-restdocs/commits/8cc4b4cd344db632b0c80ca3181226d11ad0f7de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T20:30:00Z","email":"iwan@arc-e-tect.com","name":"Iwan Eising"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T20:30:00Z","email":"iwan@arc-e-tect.com","name":"Iwan Eising"},"message":"chore(repo-hardening): add .gitignore, .gitattributes, CODEOWNERS, and security policy docs\n\nEstablishes the repository''s configuration baseline and security\ngovernance files.\n\n## .gitignore (replaces stub containing only `tmp/`)\n\nComprehensive ignore rules covering:\n- Repo structure: tmp/, worktrees/\n- Java: *.class, *.jar, *.war, *.ear and related compiled artefacts\n- Gradle: .gradle/, **/build/ with standard src exclusions\n- Node.js/Angular: node_modules/, npm/yarn debug logs, .angular/cache/\n- Credentials/secrets: .env, .env.local, .env.*.local\n- Keystores: *.p12, *.pfx, *.jks, *.ks, *.keystore, *.truststore\n- IntelliJ IDEA (root-level only, anchored with /): /.idea/* with\n  negations for .gitignore, codeStyles/, inspectionProfiles/,\n  runConfigurations/; and *.iml/*.iws/*.ipr. Using anchored patterns\n  (leading /) avoids conflicting with the .idea/* negation patterns\n  in blue-needle/.gitignore and red-thread/.gitignore, which must\n  be able to un-ignore their project-specific IDE config.\n- VS Code (root-level only, anchored with /): /.vscode/* with negations\n  for tasks.json, launch.json, extensions.json, mcp.json — same\n  rationale as IDEA above.\n- macOS: .DS_Store, ._* and related\n- Windows: Thumbs.db, Desktop.ini, $RECYCLE.BIN/\n- Logs: *.log, logs/\n- Coverage: coverage/, .nyc_output/\n- Editor temp: *.swp, *.swo, *~\n\n## .gitattributes\n\nNew root-level file enforcing cross-platform line-ending consistency:\n- * text=auto — normalize all text files on checkout\n- *.sh, gradlew → LF (required for POSIX shells and Docker)\n- *.bat, *.ps1 → CRLF (required for Windows execution)\n- Binary files (*.jar, *.png, *.jpg, *.gif, *.ico, *.zip, *.tar, *.gz,\n  *.pdf, font files) marked as binary — never converted\n\n## .github/CODEOWNERS\n\nAssigns @Arc-E-Tect as required reviewer for every file, so the\nGitHub Ruleset''s `require_code_owner_review` setting auto-requests\nthe owner''s approval on every PR.\n\n## .github/SECURITY.md\n\nGitHub-recognized security policy file. Points reporters to private\nvulnerability reporting, sets a 5-business-day SLA, and summarises\nsecurity practices (no committed secrets, pre-commit hook enforcement,\nPR-required merges to main).\n\n## ZERO_CREDENTIALS_POLICY.md\n\nDefines the mandatory no-credentials-in-VCS policy:\n- Rationale and scope\n- Correct (env var placeholder) vs incorrect (hardcoded) patterns\n- Gradle build script convention (no defaults in environment() calls)\n- Description of what the pre-commit hook blocks\n- Allowed exception file types (.example, .sample, etc.)\n- CI/CD injection pattern (GitHub Actions secrets → env vars)\n- Consequences and manual bypass warning\n\n## .idea/.gitignore\n\nIntelliJ-generated file that excludes workspace-local artefacts\n(workspace.xml, shelf/, httpRequests/, queries/, dataSources/) from\nversion control. Committing it ensures the IDE''s own ignore rules are\nshared consistently across checkouts.","tree":{"sha":"b3117382153c7a5f45fc941198722f6241cc5f97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Arc-E-Tect/sedr-wiremock-spring-restdocs/git/trees/b3117382153c7a5f45fc941198722f6241cc5f97"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Arc-E-Tect/sedr-wiremock-spring-restdocs/git/commits/8cc4b4cd344db632b0c80ca3181226d11ad0f7de","verification":{"payload":"tree b3117382153c7a5f45fc941198722f6241cc5f97\nparent a58a1948aeba25ae41966c0e99579114634aca07\nauthor Iwan Eising <iwan@arc-e-tect.com> 1779222600 +0400\ncommitter Iwan Eising <iwan@arc-e-tect.com> 1779222600 +0400\n\nchore(repo-hardening): add .gitignore, .gitattributes, CODEOWNERS, and security policy docs\n\nEstablishes the repository''s configuration baseline and security\ngovernance files.\n\n## .gitignore (replaces stub containing only `tmp/`)\n\nComprehensive ignore rules covering:\n- Repo structure: tmp/, worktrees/\n- Java: *.class, *.jar, *.war, *.ear and related compiled artefacts\n- Gradle: .gradle/, **/build/ with standard src exclusions\n- Node.js/Angular: node_modules/, npm/yarn debug logs, .angular/cache/\n- Credentials/secrets: .env, .env.local, .env.*.local\n- Keystores: *.p12, *.pfx, *.jks, *.ks, *.keystore, *.truststore\n- IntelliJ IDEA (root-level only, anchored with /): /.idea/* with\n  negations for .gitignore, codeStyles/, inspectionProfiles/,\n  runConfigurations/; and *.iml/*.iws/*.ipr. Using anchored patterns\n  (leading /) avoids conflicting with the .idea/* negation patterns\n  in blue-needle/.gitignore and red-thread/.gitignore, which must\n  be able to un-ignore their project-specific IDE config.\n- VS Code (root-level only, anchored with /): /.vscode/* with negations\n  for tasks.json, launch.json, extensions.json, mcp.json — same\n  rationale as IDEA above.\n- macOS: .DS_Store, ._* and related\n- Windows: Thumbs.db, Desktop.ini, $RECYCLE.BIN/\n- Logs: *.log, logs/\n- Coverage: coverage/, .nyc_output/\n- Editor temp: *.swp, *.swo, *~\n\n## .gitattributes\n\nNew root-level file enforcing cross-platform line-ending consistency:\n- * text=auto — normalize all text files on checkout\n- *.sh, gradlew → LF (required for POSIX shells and Docker)\n- *.bat, *.ps1 → CRLF (required for Windows execution)\n- Binary files (*.jar, *.png, *.jpg, *.gif, *.ico, *.zip, *.tar, *.gz,\n  *.pdf, font files) marked as binary — never converted\n\n## .github/CODEOWNERS\n\nAssigns @Arc-E-Tect as required reviewer for every file, so the\nGitHub Ruleset''s `require_code_owner_review` setting auto-requests\nthe owner''s approval on every PR.\n\n## .github/SECURITY.md\n\nGitHub-recognized security policy file. Points reporters to private\nvulnerability reporting, sets a 5-business-day SLA, and summarises\nsecurity practices (no committed secrets, pre-commit hook enforcement,\nPR-required merges to main).\n\n## ZERO_CREDENTIALS_POLICY.md\n\nDefines the mandatory no-credentials-in-VCS policy:\n- Rationale and scope\n- Correct (env var placeholder) vs incorrect (hardcoded) patterns\n- Gradle build script convention (no defaults in environment() calls)\n- Description of what the pre-commit hook blocks\n- Allowed exception file types (.example, .sample, etc.)\n- CI/CD injection pattern (GitHub Actions secrets → env vars)\n- Consequences and manual bypass warning\n\n## .idea/.gitignore\n\nIntelliJ-generated file that excludes workspace-local artefacts\n(workspace.xml, shelf/, httpRequests/, queries/, dataSources/) from\nversion control. Committing it ensures the IDE''s own ignore rules are\nshared consistently across checkouts.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCAAdFiEEp