NhMzE4MTIyNmQxMWFkMGY3ZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Arc-E-Tect/sedr-wiremock-spring-restdocs/commit/a58a1948aeba25ae41966c0e99579114634aca07","sha":"a58a1948aeba25ae41966c0e99579114634aca07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Arc-E-Tect/sedr-wiremock-spring-restdocs/commits/a58a1948aeba25ae41966c0e99579114634aca07"}],"sha":"8cc4b4cd344db632b0c80ca3181226d11ad0f7de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Arc-E-Tect/sedr-wiremock-spring-restdocs/commits/8cc4b4cd344db632b0c80ca3181226d11ad0f7de"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12331140?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Arc-E-Tect","id":12331140,"login":"Arc-E-Tect","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzMxMTQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Arc-E-Tect/sedr-wiremock-spring-restdocs/commits/a58a1948aeba25ae41966c0e99579114634aca07/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T20:28:50Z","email":"iwan@arc-e-tect.com","name":"Iwan Eising"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T20:28:50Z","email":"iwan@arc-e-tect.com","name":"Iwan Eising"},"message":"chore(git-hooks): add pre-commit and pre-push hooks with setup script\n\nAdd .githooks/ directory with two hooks and a setup script that\nconfigures Git to use them via `core.hooksPath`.\n\n## .githooks/pre-commit\n\nEnforces quality standards on every commit:\n- Keystore detection: blocks .p12, .pfx, .jks, .ks, .keystore,\n  .truststore files from being staged\n- Secret scanning: regex-based detection of hardcoded credentials\n  (passwords, API keys, tokens, etc.) in staged files; excludes\n  .githooks/, copilot-instructions.md, security documentation files,\n  and .example/.sample/.template files; also excludes Gradle\n  System.getenv()/project.findProperty() lookups to avoid false positives\n- UTF-8 BOM detection: prevents package.json and package-lock.json\n  with BOM markers from being committed\n- GitHub Actions workflow validation: runs actionlint on all staged\n  workflow YAML files; blocks the commit if actionlint is absent\n\n## .githooks/pre-push\n\nPrevents push to stale or already-merged branches:\n- Checks the PR state for the current branch using the gh CLI\n- Hard-blocks pushes to MERGED PR branches with remediation instructions\n- Soft-warns for CLOSED PR branches and prompts the user to continue\n- Skips the check for: main, master, maintenance, sedr_sec##_ch##\n  section/chapter branches and their hyphenated derivatives,\n  worktrees/ branches\n- Validates semantic-release config: when pushing to main and\n  release.config.js was modified, runs `semantic-release --dry-run`\n  to catch invalid configurations before they break CI\n\n## scripts/setup-hooks.sh\n\nOne-step hook installer:\n  git config core.hooksPath .githooks\n  chmod +x .githooks/pre-commit .githooks/pre-push\n\nNew contributors run this once after cloning. Documented in\n.githooks/README.md.","tree":{"sha":"633582ca5b6fe1b6d35ff310f42a018b3bf44fac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Arc-E-Tect/sedr-wiremock-spring-restdocs/git/trees/633582ca5b6fe1b6d35ff310f42a018b3bf44fac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Arc-E-Tect/sedr-wiremock-spring-restdocs/git/commits/a58a1948aeba25ae41966c0e99579114634aca07","verification":{"payload":"tree 633582ca5b6fe1b6d35ff310f42a018b3bf44fac\nparent 4dfb27f1c882cd6154ef8be66d15d1774221d935\nauthor Iwan Eising <iwan@arc-e-tect.com> 1779222530 +0400\ncommitter Iwan Eising <iwan@arc-e-tect.com> 1779222530 +0400\n\nchore(git-hooks): add pre-commit and pre-push hooks with setup script\n\nAdd .githooks/ directory with two hooks and a setup script that\nconfigures Git to use them via `core.hooksPath`.\n\n## .githooks/pre-commit\n\nEnforces quality standards on every commit:\n- Keystore detection: blocks .p12, .pfx, .jks, .ks, .keystore,\n  .truststore files from being staged\n- Secret scanning: regex-based detection of hardcoded credentials\n  (passwords, API keys, tokens, etc.) in staged files; excludes\n  .githooks/, copilot-instructions.md, security documentation files,\n  and .example/.sample/.template files; also excludes Gradle\n  System.getenv()/project.findProperty() lookups to avoid false positives\n- UTF-8 BOM detection: prevents package.json and package-lock.json\n  with BOM markers from being committed\n- GitHub Actions workflow validation: runs actionlint on all staged\n  workflow YAML files; blocks the commit if actionlint is absent\n\n## .githooks/pre-push\n\nPrevents push to stale or already-merged branches:\n- Checks the PR state for the current branch using the gh CLI\n- Hard-blocks pushes to MERGED PR branches with remediation instructions\n- Soft-warns for CLOSED PR branches and prompts the user to continue\n- Skips the check for: main, master, maintenance, sedr_sec##_ch##\n  section/chapter branches and their hyphenated derivatives,\n  worktrees/ branches\n- Validates semantic-release config: when pushing to main and\n  release.config.js was modified, runs `semantic-release --dry-run`\n  to catch invalid configurations before they break CI\n\n## scripts/setup-hooks.sh\n\nOne-step hook installer:\n  git config core.hooksPath .githooks\n  chmod +x .githooks/pre-commit .githooks/pre-push\n\nNew contributors run this once after cloning. Docum