admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/infosiragpt-ops/SiraGPT-APP/commit/a1ef40ffc292af7cf36eb5a28481d748b27272ab","node_id":"C_kwDOSiVqJ9oAKGExZWY0MGZmYzI5MmFmN2NmMzZlYjVhMjg0ODFkNzQ4YjI3MjcyYWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/infosiragpt-ops/SiraGPT-APP/commit/270b2147c8bd01e6ed1428ba19ad9f346e88600d","sha":"270b2147c8bd01e6ed1428ba19ad9f346e88600d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infosiragpt-ops/SiraGPT-APP/commits/270b2147c8bd01e6ed1428ba19ad9f346e88600d"}],"sha":"a1ef40ffc292af7cf36eb5a28481d748b27272ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infosiragpt-ops/SiraGPT-APP/commits/a1ef40ffc292af7cf36eb5a28481d748b27272ab"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/243045210?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/infosiragpt-ops/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/infosiragpt-ops/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/infosiragpt-ops/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/infosiragpt-ops/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/infosiragpt-ops","id":243045210,"login":"infosiragpt-ops","node_id":"U_kgDODnyTWg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/infosiragpt-ops/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/infosiragpt-ops/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/infosiragpt-ops/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/infosiragpt-ops/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/infosiragpt-ops/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/infosiragpt-ops","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infosiragpt-ops/SiraGPT-APP/commits/270b2147c8bd01e6ed1428ba19ad9f346e88600d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T13:48:59Z","email":"Carrerajorge8745@gmail.com","name":"infosiragpt-ops"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T13:48:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(browser): navegador integrado con pestañas, anotaciones y diseño de referencia (#981)\n\n* feat(browser): present a clean session-bound browser in agentes\n\n* fix(browser): match URL focus and add safe native gate diagnostics\n\n* fix(browser): confirm restored history and recover partial presentation\n\n* fix(browser): preserve native focus and cancel stale presentation\n\nUse public noDefaults so CDP preserves native tab focus and visibility. Pin backend Playwright and playwright-core from the previous locked 1.56.1 to 1.60.0, which exposes this option; no other dependency versions change. Replace the removed page accessibility API with public CDP AX snapshots, preserving redaction and cleanup.\n\nConfirm native tab changes and BFCache history without remembered targets. Cancel presentation if the panel closes or changes dock during explicit recovery. Wait for the real mobile resize boundary in acceptance; no added retries or increased budgets. Validated production build, bundle budget, 12997 root tests, 184 backend tests, 45 focused component/client tests and 9 local browser cases.\n\n* docs(licenses): synchronize Playwright attribution with locked versions\n\n* test(browser): retain desktop progress coverage with session-bound fixtures\n\nReproduced the legacy empty-start assertion failing before the test update. Preserve all ten cases and original timeouts; require browser session and target ownership, confirm blank start and no agent navigation replay, and exercise existing desktop controls for activity and collapse.\n\nValidation: 10 progress and 9 integrated browser cases passed with zero retries. Another 38 coding, GitHub, chat, upload and preview cases passed with zero retries. Types, UI lock, diff and secret scan passed.\n\n* ci(browser): expose only closed critical UI failure metadata\n\nLocal CI-equivalent browser and compatibility suites pass without retries, but the Linux critical UI gate still fails. Add allowlisted spec/line/status/retry annotations to identify the case without reading full CI logs or emitting test titles, errors, stacks, URLs, attachments or arbitrary paths.\n\nPreserve list reporter, all critical specs, existing retry/timeout budgets and nonzero exit handling. Eleven adversarial and real Playwright reporter tests pass on Node 24 and 26; 22 existing workflow contracts pass, YAML and secret checks pass.\n\n* test(browser): identify home failures with closed phase metadata\n\n* fix(browser): preserve omnibox focus and rebuild styles for changed sources\n\n* fix(browser): retain entered navigation while the viewport resizes\n\n* fix(browser): preserve the active page when closing a background tab\n\n* feat(browser): match reference chrome and add temporary annotations\n\n* test(browser): distinguish focus failures with closed diagnostics\n\n* fix(ci): invalidate browser styles with supported cache globs\n\n* test(ci): verify the fail-fast production build block\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Luis <luis@MacBook-Pro-de-Luis.local>","tree":{"sha":"4d9e80daf02fd50757dd6f96cdd1146cac605cb8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infosiragpt-ops/SiraGPT-APP/git/trees/4d9e80daf02fd50757dd6f96cdd1146cac605cb8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infosiragpt-ops/SiraGPT-APP/git/commits/270b2147c8bd01e6ed1428ba19ad9f346e88600d","verification":{"payload":"tree 4d9e80daf02fd50757dd6f96cdd1146cac605cb8\nparent 12c424fefc4bcb7b2e0dc34bcc13ab8adcd479ee\nauthor infosiragpt-ops <Carrerajorge8745@gmail.com> 1791035339 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791035339 -0500\n\nfeat(browser): navegador integrado con pestañas, anotaciones y diseño de referencia (#981)\n\n* feat(browser): present a clean session-bound browser in agentes\n\n* fix(browser): match URL focus and add safe native gate diagnostics\n\n* fix(browser): confirm restored history and recover partial presentation\n\n* fix(browser): preserve native focus and cancel stale presentation\n\nUse public noDefaults so CDP preserves native tab focus and visibility. Pin backend Playwright and playwright-core from the previous locked 1.56.1 to 1.60.0, which exposes this option; no other dependency versions change. Replace the removed page accessibility API with public CDP AX snapshots, preserving redaction and cleanup.\n\nConfirm native tab changes and BFCache history without remembered targets. Cancel presentation if the panel closes or changes dock during explicit recovery. Wait for the real mobile resize boundary in acceptance; no added retries or increased budgets. Validated production build, bundle budget, 12997 root tests, 184 backend tests, 45 focused component/client tests and 9 local browser cases.\n\n* docs(licenses): synchronize Playwright attribution with locked versions\n\n* test(browser): retain desktop progress coverage with session-bound fixtures\n\nReproduced the legacy empty-start assertion failing before the test update. Preserve all ten cases and original timeouts; require browser session and target ownership, confirm blank start and no agent navigation replay, and exercise existing desktop controls for activity and collapse.\n\nValidation: 10 progress and 9 integrated browser cases passed with zero retries. Another 38 coding, GitHub, chat, upload and preview cases passed with zero retries. Types, UI lock, diff and secret scan passed.\n\n* ci(browser): expose only closed critical UI failure metadata\n\nLocal CI-equivalent browser and compatibility suites pass without retries, but the Linux critical UI gate still fails. Add allowlisted spec/line/status/retry annotations to identify the case without reading full CI logs or emitting test titles, errors, stacks, URLs, attachments or arbitrary paths.\n\nPreserve list reporter, all critical specs, existing retry/timeout budgets and nonzero exit handling. Eleven adversarial and real Playwright reporter tests pass on Node 24 and 26; 22 existing workflow contracts pass, YAML and secret checks pass.\n\n* test(browser): identify home failures with closed phase metadata\n\n* fix(browser): preserve omnibox focus and rebuild styles for changed sources\n\n* fix(browser): retain entered navigation while the viewport resizes\n\n* fix(browser): preserve the active page when closing a background tab\n\n* feat(browser): match reference chrome and add temporary annotations\n\n* test(browser): distinguish focus failures with closed diagnostics\n\n* fix(ci): invalidate browser styles with supported cache globs\n\n* test(ci): verify the fail-fast production build block\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Luis <luis@MacBook-Pro-de-Luis.local>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwQfLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAli4QAIHZ9Aut8+2VAglRWn+T8UQM\ncGERAcKC+JpG93hsyeMGYobYNXlnjB1nPGZuzBeM5aCSmday0CL0rSlthHvaJ2hB\ntHfIb3s8wBzLy2fCJn4zPVOfZx/y6AivrFxpBbGTjqa22cxq19HSgGno4z6P75SO\nY1r84slNT1VplWpOgR3RJn4ATh5QKfpmLwHG86xL+encG5cOMi/yVpa6SidRhOTF\nobiZpagXUWdyzt9D/pFUaiCw0sLSOZFxaCMeSAQibKP6/x/cVfoBNAsrZz4HhLIT\nlVOKqqLMRaL5P33PuhDsjtArVq+J4kM4Mu0nE3IDR4hTccW0lxU6JZibx8rJgI+d\nkUHHvy0mZPxXL+A8djEiZw6LQ8mtfsR2UMxo3sp0Ff28Ky7HvdB0nErSlMYyX0u9\npdTZtZ2+00INadInTPBY1QvBniFMCZ+Lg4ic6YySXcgqK8Frva0e0gPVxHxmSBha\nU9fjCJnmOdyGJoeqDNl7YUmZ1WnBHwy8HQ3XAUaHWR9AKVoewQbdFOrPCey2wO1Z\nASOVdaTubREqAHx0kb3AFMzAM9Yc7sADSmgeOz6/0i3VsetEr2zh59xEh358TrRe\n0FpEJWerqE7Nc33UM2vjyGT6ppLDejJAp5vLrMowfSk4A2mz2ShkJiU+m8nK8nFy\nXcqxIOSLd7qqgyYxY34B\n=StAs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T13:49:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/infosiragpt-ops/SiraGPT-APP/commit/270b2147c8bd01e6ed1428ba19ad9f346e88600d","node_id":"C_kwDOSiVqJ9oAKDI3MGIyMTQ3YzhiZDAxZTZlZDE0MjhiYTE5YWQ5ZjM0NmU4ODYwMGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/infosiragpt-ops/SiraGPT-APP/commit/12c424fefc4bcb7b2e0dc34bcc13ab8adcd479ee","sha":"12c424fefc4bcb7b2e0dc34bcc13ab8adcd479ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infosiragpt-ops/SiraGPT-APP/commits/12c424fefc4bcb7b2e0dc34bcc13ab8adcd479ee"}],"sha":"270b2147c8bd01e6ed1428ba19ad9f346e88600d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infosiragpt-ops/SiraGPT-APP/commits/270b2147c8bd01e6ed1428ba19ad9f346e88600d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/243045210?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/infosiragpt-ops/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/infosiragpt-ops/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/infosiragpt-ops/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/infosiragpt-ops/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/infosiragpt-ops","id":243045210,"login":"infosiragpt-ops","node_id":"U_kgDODnyTWg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/infosiragpt-ops/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/infosiragpt-ops/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/infosiragpt-ops/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/infosiragpt-ops/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/infosiragpt-ops/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/infosiragpt-ops","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infosiragpt-ops/SiraGPT-APP/commits/12c424fefc4bcb7b2e0dc34bcc13ab8adcd479ee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T07:48:38Z","email":"Carrerajorge8745@gmail.com","name":"infosiragpt-ops"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T07:48:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(agentes): transcribir cualquier enlace — navegador headless, cookies y YouTube con EJS (#987)\n\nReporte de Luis: «el sistema todavía no puede transcribir el video que le di en el\nlink… tiene que entrar al video y sacar el audio sí o sí». Tres causas reales y\ntres piezas:\n\n- YouTube exige un runtime JS + el solucionador yt-dlp-ejs; el yt-dlp de apk no\n  lo trae. `backend/Dockerfile` instala `yt-dlp[default]>=2026.8` desde PyPI y\n  cada llamada usa el Node 22 del backend (`--js-runtimes node:<execPath>`).\n- Los reproductores institucionales (upn.class.com, LMS) son SPAs sin medios en\n  el HTML. `media-discovery.js` abre la página en el Chromium de la imagen\n  (Playwright) con las cookies del usuario, pulsa play y registra el\n  HLS/DASH/MP4 real; ranking, detección de muro de login, exportación de\n  cookies; postura SSRF de web_fetch en cada petición de la página.\n- Una grabación privada solo baja con la sesión del usuario.\n  `cookie-jar-store.js` guarda un cookies.txt (Netscape) por usuario, cifrado\n  con utils/encryption; solo viajan las cookies del host del enlace y nunca se\n  loguean valores.\n\n`transcribe-url-tool.js` (escalera): yt-dlp → navegador → candidato a yt-dlp con\nReferer/UA/cookies → ffmpeg directo con cabeceras. cookies.txt adjunto en el\nturno (ctx.fileIds + ownership) se usa y se guarda; `--fixup never`; si la\ndescarga por secciones falla, baja la grabación entera y recorta en local;\nel detalle de error es la última línea NO vacía de stderr. Mensajes de\n`media_login_required`/`media_unsupported_url` con los dos caminos reales\n(adjuntar el archivo / adjuntar cookies.txt una vez); línea de política del\nloop actualizada.\n\nTests: `media-discovery.test.js` (10, incluye Chromium real: SPA con HLS por JS\ndescubierto, redirección a /login = muro, filtro de cookies por host, jar\ncifrado, escalera con browser+yt-dlp y browser+ffmpeg, cookies adjuntas por\nownership, fallback de descarga entera) + `transcribe-url-tool.test.js`\nadaptado (10). Verificación manual con yt-dlp 2026.08 y ffmpeg reales contra un\nservidor local: archivo directo con rango OK de punta a punta; HLS y login\ncubiertos por el navegador real. YouTube/upn.class.com no son alcanzables\ndesde el sandbox: la prueba final es en producción.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G6q4dfjz3JYHLnjXw1rwKK\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"75939eaf04368f03a02188d91269d92d7970523f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infosiragpt-ops/SiraGPT-APP/git/trees/75939eaf04368f03a02188d91269d92d7970523f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/infosiragpt-ops/SiraGPT-APP/git/commits/12c424fefc4bcb7b2e0dc34bcc13ab8adcd479ee","verification":{"payload":"tree 75939eaf04368f03a02188d91269d92d7970523f\nparent fb9f3be8c66c91b0ab1ec006e6f2eaa9a3359148\nauthor infosiragpt-ops <Carrerajorge8745@gmail.com> 1791013718 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791013718 -0500\n\nfeat(agentes): transcribir cualquier enlace — navegador headless, cookies y YouTube con EJS (#987)\n\nReporte de Luis: «el sistema todavía no puede transcribir el video que le di en el\nlink… tiene que entrar al video y sacar el audio sí o sí». Tres causas reales y\ntres piezas:\n\n- YouTube exige un runtime JS + el solucionador yt-dlp-ejs; el yt-dlp de apk no\n  lo trae. `backend/Dockerfile` instala `yt-dlp[default]>=2026.8` desde PyPI y\n  cada llamada usa el Node 22 del backend (`--js-runtimes node:<execPath>`).\n- Los reproductores institucionales (upn.class.com, LMS) son SPAs sin medios en\n  el HTML. `media-discovery.js` abre la página en el Chromium de la imagen\n  (Playwright) con las cookies del usuario, pulsa play y registra el\n  HLS/DASH/MP4 real; ranking, detección de muro de login, exportación de\n  cookies; postura SSRF de web_fetch en cada petición de la página.\n- Una grabación privada solo baja con la sesión del usuario.\n  `cookie-jar-store.js` guarda un cookies.txt (Netscape) por usuario, cifrado\n  con utils/encryption; solo viajan las cookies del host del enlace y nunca se\n  loguean valores.\n\n`transcribe-url-tool.js` (escalera): yt-dlp → navegador → candidato a yt-dlp con\nReferer/UA/cookies → ffmpeg directo con cabeceras. cookies.txt adjunto en el\nturno (ctx.fileIds + ownership) se usa y se guarda; `--fixup never`; si la\ndescarga por secciones falla, baja la grabación entera y recorta en local;\nel detalle de error es la última línea NO vacía de stderr. Mensajes de\n`media_login_required`/`media_unsupported_url` con los dos caminos reales\n(adjuntar el archivo / adjuntar cookies.txt una vez); línea de política del\nloop actualizada.\n\nTests: `media-discovery.test.js` (10, incluye Chromium real: SPA con HLS por JS\ndescubierto, redirección a /login = muro, filtro de cookies por host, jar\ncifrado, escalera con browser+yt-dlp y browser+ffmpeg, cookies adjuntas por\nownership, fallback de descarga entera) + `transcribe-url-tool.test.js`\nadaptado (10). Verificación manual con yt-dlp 2026.08 y ffmpeg reales contra un\nservidor local: archivo directo con rango OK de punta a punta; HLS y login\ncubiertos por el navegador real. YouTube/upn.class.com no son alcanzables\ndesde el sandbox: la prueba final es en producción.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https: